\nweb test:native-pair: + Use the safe SDK when expected failures should be returned as values instead of\nweb test:native-pair: + rejected Promises.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Call \\`TaxKit.safe.calculate\\` [#call-taxkitsafecalculate]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { TaxKit } from \"@taxkit/sdk\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + const result = await TaxKit.safe.calculate(au.calculations.annualIncomeTax, {\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + if (result._tag === \"TaxKitSuccess\") {\nweb test:native-pair: +   console.log(result.value.liability.cents);\nweb test:native-pair: + }\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + if (result._tag === \"TaxKitFailure\") {\nweb test:native-pair: +   console.error(result.error._tag);\nweb test:native-pair: + }\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The result is either \\`TaxKitSuccess\\` with the calculator report or\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`TaxKitFailure\\` with an SDK-owned error value.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Call AU safe helpers [#call-au-safe-helpers]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + const result = await au.incomeTax.safe.annual({\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxableIncome: aud(Cents.make(9_000_000)),\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## When to use it [#when-to-use-it]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use the safe facade when your application already models expected failures as\nweb test:native-pair: + data, or when you want to handle schema decode errors in the same branch as\nweb test:native-pair: + calculation failures. A client that has been closed returns \\`TaxKitFailure\\` with\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`TaxKitClientDisposedError\\` in \\`result.error.error\\`. Await \\`client.dispose()\\` when\nweb test:native-pair: + finished; the [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk) shows a \\`try\\`/\\`finally\\` example.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use \\`TaxKit.calculate\\` when rejected Promises fit your existing control flow.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related pages [#related-pages]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Schemas](/sdk/schemas)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Type safety](/sdk/type-safety)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`safe-sdk`,content:`Use the safe SDK when expected failures should be returned as values instead of\nweb test:native-pair: + rejected Promises.`},{heading:`call-taxkitsafecalculate`,content:\"The result is either `TaxKitSuccess` with the calculator report or\\n`TaxKitFailure` with an SDK-owned error value.\"},{heading:`when-to-use-it`,content:\"Use the safe facade when your application already models expected failures as\\ndata, or when you want to handle schema decode errors in the same branch as\\ncalculation failures. A client that has been closed returns `TaxKitFailure` with\\n`TaxKitClientDisposedError` in `result.error.error`. Await `client.dispose()` when\\nfinished; the Plain SDK shows a `try`/`finally` example.\"},{heading:`when-to-use-it`,content:\"Use `TaxKit.calculate` when rejected Promises fit your existing control flow.\"},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Plain SDK`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Schemas`},{heading:`related-pages`,content:`Type safety`}],head