 break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;\"><span class=\"nodeLabel\"><p>New tax formula, threshold or source-backed derivation</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class=\"node default\" id=\"mermaid-0-flowchart-Calculator-3\" data-look=\"classic\" transform=\"translate(758, 175)\"><rect class=\"basic label-container\" style=\"\" x=\"-130\" y=\"-39\" width=\"260\" height=\"78\"/><g class=\"label\" style=\"\" transform=\"translate(-100, -24)\"><rect/><foreignObject width=\"200\" height=\"48\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;\"><span class=\"nodeLabel\"><p>New public calculation goal or report</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class=\"node default\" id=\"mermaid-0-flowchart-Year-4\" data-look=\"classic\" transform=\"translate(1068, 175)\"><rect class=\"basic label-container\" style=\"\" x=\"-130\" y=\"-39\" width=\"260\" height=\"78\"/><g class=\"label\" style=\"\" transform=\"translate(-100, -24)\"><rect/><foreignObject width=\"200\" height=\"48\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;\"><span class=\"nodeLabel\"><p>New tax year or parameter period</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class=\"node default\" id=\"mermaid-0-flowchart-Result-5\" data-look=\"classic\" transform=\"translate(1378, 175)\"><rect class=\"basic label-container\" style=\"\" x=\"-130\" y=\"-39\" width=\"260\" height=\"78\"/><g class=\"label\" style=\"\" transform=\"translate(-100, -24)\"><rect/><foreignObject width=\"200\" height=\"48\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: table; white-space: break-spaces; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center; width: 200px;\"><span class=\"nodeLabel\"><p>A result disagrees with a source or known scenario</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g><g class=\"node default\" id=\"mermaid-0-flowchart-Evidence-6\" data-look=\"classic\" transform=\"translate(758, 291)\"><rect class=\"basic label-container\" style=\"\" x=\"-108.2578125\" y=\"-27\" width=\"216.515625\" height=\"54\"/><g class=\"label\" style=\"\" transform=\"translate(-78.2578125, -12)\"><rect/><foreignObject width=\"156.515625\" height=\"24\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" style=\"display: table-cell; white-space: nowrap; line-height: 1.5; max-width: 200px; text-align: center;\"><span class=\"nodeLabel\"><p>PR evidence checklist</p></span></div></foreignObject></g></g></g></g></g><defs><filter id=\"mermaid-0-drop-shadow\" height=\"130%\" width=\"130%\"><feDropShadow dx=\"4\" dy=\"4\" stdDeviation=\"0\" flood-opacity=\"0.06\" flood-color=\"#000000\"/></filter></defs><defs><filter id=\"mermaid-0-drop-shadow-small\" height=\"150%\" width=\"150%\"><feDropShadow dx=\"2\" dy=\"2\" stdDeviation=\"0\" flood-opacity=\"0.06\" flood-color=\"#000000\"/></filter></defs><linearGradient id=\"mermaid-0-gradient\" gradientUnits=\"objectBoundingBox\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"0%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"hsl(0, 0%, 83.3333333333%)\" stop-opacity=\"1\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"hsl(0, 0%, 88.9215686275%)\" stop-opacity=\"1\"/></linearGradient></svg>\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + | If you want to                                                                      | Start with                                                       | Owning package                                                                                    |\nweb test:native-pair: + | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Add an input fact, derived fact or question prompt                                  | [Add a fact](/contributing/add-a-fact)                           | Usually \\`@taxkit/core\\` for shared descriptors, or the owning rule package for rule-specific facts |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Add or change a tax formula, threshold, parameter table or source-backed derivation | [Add a rule](/contributing/add-a-rule)                           | \\`@taxkit/rules-au-pay\\`, \\`@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax\\` or \\`@taxkit/rules-au-stsl\\`                  |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Add a public calculation goal, request context or report shape                      | [Add a calculator](/contributing/add-a-calculator)               | Rule package for the calculator program, \\`@taxkit/calculators\\` for reusable orchestration         |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Add support for another tax year                                                    | [Add a tax year](/contributing/add-a-tax-year)                   | The rule package that owns the parameter table and calculator context                             |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Fix a reported incorrect result                                                     | [Fix an incorrect result](/contributing/fix-an-incorrect-result) | The package that owns the failing fact, rule, parameter table or calculator                       |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Change HTTP endpoint shape or SDK helper shape                                      | [Backward compatibility](/contributing/backward-compatibility)   | \\`@taxkit/api-http\\` for transport contracts, \\`@taxkit/sdk\\` for SDK facades                         |\nweb test:native-pair: + | Prepare a reviewable pull request                                                   | [PR evidence checklist](/contributing/pr-evidence-checklist)     | The package you changed, plus public docs when behaviour changes                                  |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Boundary rule [#boundary-rule]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + HTTP and SDK layers must not hide tax business logic. Put calculator lookup,\nweb test:native-pair: + fact decoding, rule execution, graph assembly and expected calculator errors\nweb test:native-pair: + in the owning engine, rule or calculator package. HTTP handlers can translate\nweb test:native-pair: + route input and status envelopes. SDK helpers can adapt developer-facing calls\nweb test:native-pair: + to canonical calculator requests.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + For deeper boundaries, read\nweb test:native-pair: + [Package ownership](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/docs/architecture/package-ownership.md) and\nweb test:native-pair: + [API and SDK](https://github.com/crcorbett/taxkit/blob/a151e51e8a30247526fa93412df046955846eca4/docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md).\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Next step [#next-step]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Open the guide that matches your intent, then keep\nweb test:native-pair: + [PR evidence checklist](/contributing/pr-evidence-checklist) open while you work.\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Use this page when you know the behaviour you want to change, but not the\nweb test:native-pair: + owning package or review evidence yet.`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`If you want to`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Start with`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Owning package`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add an input fact, derived fact or question prompt`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add a fact`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:\"Usually `@taxkit/core` for shared descriptors, or the owning rule package for rule-specific facts\"},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add or change a tax formula, threshold, parameter table or source-backed derivation`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add a rule`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:\"`@taxkit/rules-au-pay`, `@taxkit/rules-au-income-tax` or `@taxkit/rules-au-stsl`\"},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add a public calculation goal, request context or report shape`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add a calculator`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:\"Rule package for the calculator program, `@taxkit/calculators` for reusable orchestration\"},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add support for another tax year`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Add a tax year`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`The rule package that owns the parameter table and calculator context`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Fix a reported incorrect result`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Fix an incorrect result`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`The package that owns the failing fact, rule, parameter table or calculator`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Change HTTP endpoint shape or SDK helper shape`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Backward compatibility`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:\"`@taxkit/api-http` for transport contracts, `@taxkit/sdk` for SDK facades\"},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`Prepare a reviewable pull request`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`PR evidence checklist`},{heading:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`The package you changed, plus public docs when behaviour changes`},{heading:`boundary-rule`,content:`HTTP and SDK layers must not hide tax business logic. Put calculator lookup,\nweb test:native-pair: + fact decoding, rule execution, graph assembly and expected calculator errors\nweb test:native-pair: + in the owning engine, rule or calculator package. HTTP handlers can translate\nweb test:native-pair: + route input and status envelopes. SDK helpers can adapt developer-facing calls\nweb test:native-pair: + to canonical calculator requests.`},{heading:`boundary-rule`,content:`For deeper boundaries, read\nweb test:native-pair: + Package ownership and\nweb test:native-pair: + API and SDK.`},{heading:`next-step`,content:`Open the guide that matches your intent, then keep\nweb test:native-pair: + PR evidence checklist open while you work.`}],headings:[{id:`what-are-you-changing`,content:`What are you changing?`},{id:`boundary-rule`,content:`Boundary rule`},{id:`next-step`,content:`Next step`}]},a=[{depth:1,url:`#what-are-you-changing`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`What are you changing?`})},{depth:2,url:`#boundary-rule`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Boundary rule`})},{depth:2,url:`#next-step`,title:(0,t.jsx)(t.Fragment,{children:`Next step`})}];function o(e){let n={a:`a`,circle:`circle`,code:`code`,defs:`defs`,div:`div`,feDropShadow:`feDropShadow`,filter:`filter`,foreignObject:`foreignObject`,g:`g`,h1:`h1`,h2:`h2`,linearGradient:`linearGradient`,marker:`marker`,p:`p`,path:`path`,polygon:`polygon`,rect:`rect`,span:`span`,stop:`stop`,style:`style`,svg:`svg`,table:`table`,tbody:`tbody`,td:`td`,th:`th`,thead:`thead`,tr:`tr`,...e.components};return(0,t.jsxs)(t.Fragment,{children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.h1,{id:`what-are-you-changing`,children:`What are you changing?`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:`Use this page when you know the behaviour you want to change, but not the\nweb test:native-pair: + owning package or review evidence yet.`}),`\nweb test:native-pair: + `,(0,t.jsx)(n.p,{children:(0,t.jsxs)(n.svg,{id:`mermaid-0`,width:`100%`,xmlns:`http://www.w3.org/2000/svg`,xmlnsXlink:`http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink`,className:`flowchart`,style:{maxWidth:`1516px`},viewBox:`0 0 1516 326`,role:`graphics-document document`,\"aria-roledescription\":`flowchart-v2`,children:[(0,t.jsx)(n.style,{children:`#mermaid-0{font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;fill:#000000;}@keyframes edge-animation-frame{from{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}@keyframes dash{to{stroke-dashoffset:0;}}#mermai