 path keeps the calculation in-process and avoids HTTP transport.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Before you start [#before-you-start]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * Install the SDK with [Install the SDK](/start/install-the-sdk).\nweb test:native-pair: + * Use a TypeScript runtime that can import the SDK.\nweb test:native-pair: + * Represent money in cents with \\`aud\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Steps [#steps]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + 1. Import \\`aud\\`, \\`GrossPay\\` and the AU SDK helper.\nweb test:native-pair: + 2. Build the canonical gross pay fact.\nweb test:native-pair: + 3. Call \\`au.pay.takeHomePay\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: + 4. Check user input before the call and handle calculation failures with the\nweb test:native-pair: +    safe helper.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Example [#example]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import { Cents, aud } from \"@taxkit/core/primitives\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { GrossPay } from \"@taxkit/rules-au-pay\";\nweb test:native-pair: + import { au } from \"@taxkit/sdk/au\";\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + const report = await au.pay.takeHomePay({\nweb test:native-pair: +   grossPay: new GrossPay({\nweb test:native-pair: +     amount: aud(Cents.make(165_400)),\nweb test:native-pair: +     period: \"weekly\",\nweb test:native-pair: +   }),\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxFreeThresholdClaimed: true,\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + console.log({\nweb test:native-pair: +   kind: report._tag,\nweb test:native-pair: +   netPayCents: report.netPay.cents,\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Verify the result [#verify-the-result]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Expected output:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`json\nweb test:native-pair: + { \"kind\": \"TakeHomePayReport\", \"netPayCents\": 130100 }\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + This matches the current SDK test fixture for weekly gross pay of $1,654.00.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Handle errors [#handle-errors]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Check untrusted input as shown in [Handle validation errors](/guides/handle-validation-errors).\nweb test:native-pair: + Then use the safe helper when you want expected calculation failures as values:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + const result = await au.pay.safe.takeHomePay({\nweb test:native-pair: +   grossPay: new GrossPay({\nweb test:native-pair: +     amount: aud(Cents.make(165_400)),\nweb test:native-pair: +     period: \"weekly\",\nweb test:native-pair: +   }),\nweb test:native-pair: +   taxFreeThresholdClaimed: true,\nweb test:native-pair: + });\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + if (result._tag === \"TaxKitFailure\") {\nweb test:native-pair: +   console.error(result.error.message);\nweb test:native-pair: + }\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related pages [#related-pages]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Plain SDK](/sdk/plain-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Calculators](/concepts/calculators)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`calculate-australian-take-home-pay`,content:`Use this guide when you need a pay-period take-home amount from TypeScript.\nweb test:native-pair: + The SDK path keeps the calculation in-process and avoids HTTP transport.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Install the SDK with Install the SDK.`},{heading:`before-you-start`,content:`Use a TypeScript runtime that can import the SDK.`},{heading:`before-yo