\\`CalculatorRunRequest\\`        | Public calculator run payload shape.          |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunServiceRequest\\` | Service-level request with the calculator id. |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorRunResponse\\`       | Canonical run response shape.                 |\nweb test:native-pair: + | \\`CalculatorServiceError\\`      | Expected calculator service failure union.    |\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Safe-result schemas [#safe-result-schemas]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + The SDK also exports safe-result and error schemas:\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`ts\nweb test:native-pair: + import {\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitClientDisposedError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitClientDisposeError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitFailure,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitSchemaDecodeError,\nweb test:native-pair: +   TaxKitSuccess,\nweb test:native-pair: + } from \"@taxkit/sdk/schemas\";\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`\\`\\`\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + Use these when you persist, inspect or validate results returned by\nweb test:native-pair: + \\`TaxKit.safe.calculate\\`. \\`TaxKitClientDisposedError\\` describes calculation calls\nweb test:native-pair: + after a client closes. \\`TaxKitClientDisposeError\\` describes a safe cleanup failure\nweb test:native-pair: + from \\`dispose()\\`.\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + ## Related pages [#related-pages]\nweb test:native-pair: +\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Safe SDK](/sdk/safe-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Effect SDK](/sdk/effect-sdk)\nweb test:native-pair: + * [Type safety](/sdk/type-safety)\nweb test:native-pair: + `,i={contents:[{heading:`schemas`,content:`Use SDK schema exports when your application needs the canonical calculator run\nweb test:native-pair: + contracts or safe-result error shapes.`},{heading:`import-schemas`,content:\"These names are re-exported from th