csMarkdown` and `SearchDocsPages`.\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-206-The combined server group admits these alongside the existing nine calculator\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:207:procedures. Calculator clients and revision 4 stay unchanged; documentation\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:208:calls require their own revision 1 and fail with `DocsRpcVersionMismatch` during\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-209-version skew. There is no automatic retry or backend fallback.\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-210-\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:211:`DocsRpcClientLive` takes the existing checked API origin and caller-supplied\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-212-HttpClient. Each call owns its native receive-loop scope, the ten-second whole\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-213-reply deadline and the same private 2 MiB byte reader as calculator calls. That\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-214-reader stops before an oversized tail, releases request/body resources and\n--\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-218-\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-219-Handlers capture the supplied `ContentService` once and return its immutable\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-220-values. Public missing-page and source-search errors use the content owner's\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:221:fixed errors. The documentation procedure defect is a fixed literal; the native\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-222-global fatal path retains its already qualified fixed literal. Internal source\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-223-diagnostics and raw Causes are not response values. The native API supplies the\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-224-same generated catalogue for HTTP and RPC. This package imports only compiled\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-225-content contracts, with no MDX compiler or source collection dependency.\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-226-\npackages/api/rpc/README.md:227:Focused documentation tests cover all four calls, valid and incompatible\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-228-versions, safe expected/global/procedure failures, damaged replies, unrelated\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-229-adapter defects, exact/oversized encoded byte limits, headers/body deadlines,\npackages/api/rpc/README.md-230-earlier cancellation, scope close and transport policy. The actual native pair\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":12208},"formatted_output":"docs/architecture/package-ownership.md-32-- `packages/api/http`\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-33-- `packages/api/rpc`\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-34-: Private compiled native Effect RPC transport. It owns separately versioned\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:35:  calculator and documentation procedures, thin named service handlers, checked POST/JSON ingress and\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-36-  caller-scoped private client Layers. Calculator/content Schemas remain with\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-37-  their existing owners. Explicit test-only composition is separate; no app\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-38-  runtime or backend fallback belongs here. T003 app-host composition is locally accepted; T009 exported tracing remains open.\n--\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-136-  full T003 acceptance and the other calculator pages remain in progress.\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-137-\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-138-`apps/docs`\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md:139:: Implemented public documentation app. It owns TanStack Start routes, the\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-140-  docs app shell, route loaders, navigation presentation and app-local\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-141-  MDX component composition, Schema-decoded build target, Cloudflare Vite\ndocs/architecture/package-ownership.md-142-  configuration, static-asset headers and local built-Worker proof. It\n--\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-20-## Main areas\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-21-\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-22-`apps/docs`\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:23:: Public documentation site. It owns the TanStack Start route runtime, app\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-24-  shell, app-specific MDX component composition and browser rendering.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-25-\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-26-`packages/docs-content/content`\n--\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-63-  Standard Schema bridging, the generic source service and live/test Layers,\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-64-  and generic MDX render primitives.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-65-\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:66:`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-67-: Machine-readable separation between public content, maintainer documents,\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:68:generated artifacts, and authored SDK documentation. It validates accepted\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-69-public-status representation and navigation ownership without claiming runtime\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-70-or external availability.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-71-\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:72:`tools/documentation/catalogue.runtime.ts`\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-73-: Local accepted-catalogue build command (`bun run docs:catalogue`). It checks\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-74-version-two records and exact source hashes before and after MDX processing,\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-75-omits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\n--\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-80-package build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-81-browser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-82-checked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:83:HTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-84-processed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-85-refinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. Replacement Website routes and discovery remain T005 work.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-86-\n--\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-133-- Do not document private downstream product strategy here.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-134-- Link to canonical architecture docs rather than duplicating them.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-135-- Treat old planning material as historical until revalidated.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:136:- Use [Documentation style](../standards/documentation-style.md) and the\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-137-  related standards suite before writing or reviewing public docs.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-138-- Keep public MDX pages task-first. Use architecture docs for durable\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-139-  ownership and runtime detail.\n--\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-141-  frontmatter, navigation coverage, source-text policy, local link, MDX\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-142-  component allowlist, examples and OpenAPI reference checks.\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-143-- `draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate public\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:144:  documentation; it is not accepted-current truth, publication, deployment,\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-145-  external availability, correctness, or user visibility. `published` means\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md:146:  explicitly accepted current public documentation; it still does not establish\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-147-  runtime or external availability. Preserve draft pages unless explicit\ndocs/architecture/content-and-posts.md-148-  page-level acceptan