fixed safe values; expected/version errors retain checked identity. A source-built damaged valid-JSON reply must restore a checked error through the genuine Website binding, with real Chromium editing and no replay. Positive fixed host logs omit the marker and pay values. Removal of each native encoder or the owned reply decoder must fail the saved test, followed by exact restoration and fresh dependency/artifact builds. Controlled API roots retain the real calculation/encoding and delay headers or the remaining body for twelve seconds. Actual generated clients must hit the ten-second deadline; Chromium must observe request abort after deadline, editing and actual Back route departure. Removing deadline or edit interruption fails the saved test; exact restoration and fresh builds pass. Pay-value checks inspect emitted log messages; private text checks inspect the whole record. Actual native mock-plan properties and saved real CLI state must contain the disabled collection policy; removing the API graph property fails the saved state Schema after runtime checks. These are declared-state checks, not cloud upload or exported-row proof. An actual successful browser answer survives edits, controlled unavailable retry and invalid form without being presented as current. Reverting figures makes no request and still needs one explicit real RPC to clear the stale message. Actual Worker-generated successful submission HTML hydrates without replay and retains its answer through editing and failed retry. The additional pages must independently return both known results via real API artifacts; no calculation fixture supplies them. Each page starts without the previous calculator's answer. Saved forms and report identity are checked together. Exact browser locator fill admissions have actual CLI positive and neighbouring-application negative fixtures. The size oracle uses multi-byte text below 65536 characters but above 65536 encoded bytes at both API paths and all three form paths. API boundary fixtures also accept exactly 65536 bytes and reject progressive streams without reading their tail. The bounded private client must classify an actual native 413 as the checked request-size error. Valid native calculator/catalogue replies at exactly 2 MiB succeed; over-limit streams stop before the tail and release. Status fixtures prove request-controller abort, safe serialized guidance and one call only. Six restored checked error variants hydrate with their guidance and no new calculation. The built shared-work fixture reaches eight calculations across one HTTP call and a seven-item RPC batch, refuses extra HTTP/SSR/public browser work, retains manual-retry guidance with no edit replay, emits checked HTTP 504/RPC timeouts at five seconds and reaches cleanup. The actual generated client preserves timeout identity. Direct scoped tests prove cancelled/failed place reuse and independent instance pools; timers do not claim forced CPU pre-emption. The owning native pair also reads detail/schema/graph/facts/rules/jurisdictions/tax years from the actual API artifact. The shared RPC corpus proves decoder, size, status, deadline, interruption and old-revision rejection for every named call. Documentation assertions inspect actual initial HTML for every page before independent Chromium navigation. Three source-built API variants retain valid checked pages but change Markdown, metadata or module identity; cold Website SSR and the actual native GET must detect each mismatch. A genuine server-function response is damaged in the browser to prove restoration rejects it. The API artifact must positively contain the executable calculator service identity and browser chunks must omit it; accepted documentation prose cannot stand in for an engine marker. Full-page images supplement functional observations only.\",\n      \"environment\": \"Local TaxKit checkout, native workerd and Chromium\",\n      \"authority\": \"none\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/doc