{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:14:22.309Z","ordinal":48997,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-023eec19-4f6a-4a2e-8ef6-75809171c4ac","process_id":"98110","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'native mock|actual.*fixture' tools/oxlint/no-route-transport-restore-outside-consumers.test.ts | head -20 && sed -n '185,219p' docs/architecture/effect-services.md && rg -n -C 3 'route-transport' tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts | head -60"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'native mock|actual.*fixture' tools/oxlint/no-route-transport-restore-outside-consumers.test.ts","query":"native mock|actual.*fixture","path":"no-route-transport-restore-outside-consumers.test.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '185,219p' docs/architecture/effect-services.md","name":"effect-services.md","path":"docs/architecture/effect-services.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n -C 3 route-transport tools/oxlint/portable-rules.test.ts","query":"route-transport","path":"portable-rules.test.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"narrow generated-collection adapter at construction, contains unknown provider\noutput plus promise and throw handling, and emits safe tagged errors.\n`@taxkit/docs-content` supplies the TaxKit collection adapter and decodes the\ngeneric value into its canonical content Schemas. Neither package executes a\nruntime; `apps/docs` composes the Layers and runs the server Effect.\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"narrow generated-collection adapter at construction, contains unknown provider\noutput plus promise and throw handling, and emits safe tagged errors.\n`@taxkit/docs-content` supplies the TaxKit collection adapter and decodes the\ngeneric value into its canonical content Schemas. Neither package executes a\nruntime; `apps/docs` composes the Layers and runs the server Effect.\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7417},"formatted_output":"narrow generated-collection adapter at construction, contains unknown provider\noutput plus promise and throw handling, and emits safe tagged errors.\n`@taxkit/docs-content` supplies the TaxKit collection adapter and decodes the\ngeneric value into its canonical content Schemas. Neither package executes a\nruntime; `apps/docs` composes the Layers and runs the server Effect.\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\n"},"started_at_ms":1791306862309,"completed_at_ms":1791306862309}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:14:22.375Z","ordinal":48998,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11235-8f27-7f92-9a7a-17522f1cdb8c","call_id":"call_971745b1e057455d90e0cac9d8d7e993","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"cde3f2\",\"wall_time_seconds\":1.002056459,\"session_id\":56677,\"original_token_count\":265,\"output\":\"132:    \\\"verification\\\": \\\"bun run check:skills:types && bun run check:oxlint:types && bun run check:repository-paths:types && bun run check:repository-paths && bun run check:harness-governance && bun run check:quality-workflow:types && bun run check:quality-workflow && bun run check:docs:types && bun run check:harness-foundation-epoch:types && bun run check:docs && bun run check:runbooks && bun run check:effect-language-service && bun run check:docs-deployment:types && bun run check:docs-deployment-tools:types && bun run check:docs-deployment && bun run check:docs-deployment-automation && bun run test:docs-deployment && bun run lint && bun run format:check && bun run test:skills && bun run test:hgi-206 && bun run test:quality-workflow && bun run knip && bun run knip:production && bun run check-types && bun run sdk:test:browser && bun run web:test:browser && bun run --filter=web check:worker-types && bun run web:test:native-pair\\\",\\n137:    \\\"web:test:native-pair\\\": \\\"bun run --filter=web build:native-pair && bun run --filter=web test:native-pair\\\",\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"dfa845\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007417,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":579,\"output\":\"narrow generated-collection adapter at construction, contains unknown provider\\noutput plus promise and throw handling, and emits safe tagged errors.\\n`@taxkit/docs-content` supplies the TaxKit collection adapter and decodes the\\ngeneric value into its canonical content Schemas. Neither package executes a\\nruntime; `apps/docs` composes the Layers and runs the server Effect.\\n\\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\\n\\n## Runtime composition\\n\\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\\n\\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\\n\\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791306862.375634}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
