{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:32:52.957Z","ordinal":49336,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-53cffc3c-66a1-4fda-b01c-a480e25223c9","process_id":"11179","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'error TS|error:' /private/tmp/dev76-search-query-g-web-types.log; sed -n '450,565p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json; sed -n '75,104p' docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md; sed -n '190,220p' docs/architecture/effect-services.md; rg -n 'Website.*documentation|native documentation|connect.*docs|Website page|Search' docs/architecture/frontend.md docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md | tail -25; sed -n '320,390p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'error TS|error:' /private/tmp/dev76-search-query-g-web-types.log","query":"error TS|error:","path":"dev76-search-query-g-web-types.log"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '450,565p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json","name":"clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json","path":"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '75,104p' docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md","name":"content-and-posts.md","path":"docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '190,220p' docs/architecture/effect-services.md","name":"effect-services.md","path":"docs/architecture/effect-services.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Website.*documentation|native documentation|connect.*docs|Website page|Search' docs/architecture/frontend.md docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md","query":"Website.*documentation|native documentation|connect.*docs|Website page|Search","path":"frontend.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '320,390p' docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md","name":"clean-slate-foundation.md","path":"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"54:web check-types: src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx(132,33): error TS2375: Type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, undefined, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, undefined>' is not assignable to type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, ({ context, abortController, serverContext }: LoaderFnContext<Register, any, \"__root__\", {}, {}, ... 4 more ..., undefined>) => Promise<...>, ... 4 more ..., undefined>' with 'exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true'. Consider adding 'undefined' to the types of the target's properties.\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run changeset:status\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n        \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n        \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n        \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n        \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-schema-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-fallible-domain-values.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-parameter-table-relationships.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-core-ambient-type-portability.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-absence-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-request-absence.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-contract-closeout.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-shared-rate-admission.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-006\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n        \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n        \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n        \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n        \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n        \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n        \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n        \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n        \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n        \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n        \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n        \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run docs:validate\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n        \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n        \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n        \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n        \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n        \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\nomits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\nand writes ignored `.source/public-catalogue.json` only on success. No accepted\npages is a failure. Source acceptance is recorded independently for each page\nand navigation in the owner policy's exact bindings. Reviewed byte hashes\nprevent a later edit from silently inheriting acceptance. The docs-content\npackage build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\nbrowser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\nchecked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\nHTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\nprocessed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\nrefinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. The\nreplacement Website renders accepted pages using that private connection and\nbrowser-safe compiled presentation. Search interaction, discovery and old-app\nretirement remain T005 work.\n\n`docs/architecture`\n: Durable implementation architecture.\n\n`docs/product-specs`\n: Current product/spec intent for repo development.\n\n## Public docs graph\n\n```ts\nProduction: public docs request\n\nbrowser\n  -> apps/docs route\n    -> apps/docs route boundary schema\n    -> DocsContentService\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\ninterruption/scopes release resources.\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:1454:### Native Website documentation qualification\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:378:This does not yet connect Website documentation loaders or replace its routes.\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:382:## Replacement Website documentation composition\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:385:four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations. One server\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:420:reading without JavaScript. Search and discovery are later T005 work. The\n`CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` is a required positive decimal string selected by\nthe operator for that account and stage. No cloud value is invented. The guarded\ndisposable development root explicitly selects `local-emulator`, one shared\nloopback allowance and its isolated local namespace. Hosted composition defaults\nto `edge`; the local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\nMissing hosted identity still fails safely. The native RPC does not transfer an\nexplicit AbortSignal on the pinned runtime: client cancellation stops local\nwaiting, while the existing API operation budget bounds remote work. No\nexperimental platform flag or dependency upgrade is introduced.\n\n\nKeep owning Schemas, schema-derived types, branded identities, checked semantic\nConfig, services, Layers and tagged errors. Core ledger types now infer from their Schema;\nrecursive trace types share one field owner and annotate only children. Existing\nencoded bytes, field order and omission/undefined behaviour stay unchanged.\nThis type-owner slice does not complete the remaining fallible constructors,\nsemantic Option migration or table relationship checks. Decode unknown representations once\nat their true boundary and encode outward values. Keep Effects lazy and flat;\nkeep one-use mapping and error logic beside the operation. Separate contracts,\nlive Layers, test Layers and application execution. Provider adapters expose\nnamed operations and immediately decode replies; no raw SDK client, generic\ncallback, `instanceof` policy or primitive secret configuration escapes.\nPublic service operations normally return a closed\n`Effect.Effect<Success, DomainError, never>`; dependencies are supplied when\ntheir Layer is built. Public effectful methods use named `Effect.fn`; private\nwork stays in the caller's span unless it owns a separate external operation.\nInfer types from one owning Schema and reuse whole-record checks as well as\nfields/brands. Do not re-decode checked internal values, mirror primitive\nrefinements or JSON-encode internal cache keys. New constrained values use the\nowner's fallible constructor with named failures. Convert semantic absence to\nOption while preserving any historical missing/null encoding and source hashes\nat their actual codec boundary.\n\nCooper requires a stronger functional policy than the skill's minimum:\n\n- Bind owned values with `const`; no `let`/`var`, reassignment, increment/decrement,\n  property/index writes, deletion, mutable class fields or in-place updates.\n  This includes short-lived local builders and test observation arrays.\n- Domain and service values are readonly Schema-derived records, readonly\n  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"54:web check-types: src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx(132,33): error TS2375: Type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, undefined, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, undefined>' is not assignable to type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, ({ context, abortController, serverContext }: LoaderFnContext<Register, any, \"__root__\", {}, {}, ... 4 more ..., undefined>) => Promise<...>, ... 4 more ..., undefined>' with 'exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true'. Consider adding 'undefined' to the types of the target's properties.\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run changeset:status\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n        \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n        \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n        \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n        \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-schema-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-fallible-domain-values.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-parameter-table-relationships.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-core-ambient-type-portability.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-absence-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-request-absence.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-contract-closeout.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-shared-rate-admission.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-006\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n        \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n        \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n        \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n        \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n        \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n        \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n        \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n        \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n        \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n        \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n        \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run docs:validate\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n        \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n        \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n        \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n        \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n        \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\nomits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\nand writes ignored `.source/public-catalogue.json` only on success. No accepted\npages is a failure. Source acceptance is recorded independently for each page\nand navigation in the owner policy's exact bindings. Reviewed byte hashes\nprevent a later edit from silently inheriting acceptance. The docs-content\npackage build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\nbrowser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\nchecked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\nHTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\nprocessed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\nrefinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. The\nreplacement Website renders accepted pages using that private connection and\nbrowser-safe compiled presentation. Search interaction, discovery and old-app\nretirement remain T005 work.\n\n`docs/architecture`\n: Durable implementation architecture.\n\n`docs/product-specs`\n: Current product/spec intent for repo development.\n\n## Public docs graph\n\n```ts\nProduction: public docs request\n\nbrowser\n  -> apps/docs route\n    -> apps/docs route boundary schema\n    -> DocsContentService\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\ninterruption/scopes release resources.\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:1454:### Native Website documentation qualification\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:378:This does not yet connect Website documentation loaders or replace its routes.\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:382:## Replacement Website documentation composition\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:385:four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations. One server\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:420:reading without JavaScript. Search and discovery are later T005 work. The\n`CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` is a required positive decimal string selected by\nthe operator for that account and stage. No cloud value is invented. The guarded\ndisposable development root explicitly selects `local-emulator`, one shared\nloopback allowance and its isolated local namespace. Hosted composition defaults\nto `edge`; the local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\nMissing hosted identity still fails safely. The native RPC does not transfer an\nexplicit AbortSignal on the pinned runtime: client cancellation stops local\nwaiting, while the existing API operation budget bounds remote work. No\nexperimental platform flag or dependency upgrade is introduced.\n\n\nKeep owning Schemas, schema-derived types, branded identities, checked semantic\nConfig, services, Layers and tagged errors. Core ledger types now infer from their Schema;\nrecursive trace types share one field owner and annotate only children. Existing\nencoded bytes, field order and omission/undefined behaviour stay unchanged.\nThis type-owner slice does not complete the remaining fallible constructors,\nsemantic Option migration or table relationship checks. Decode unknown representations once\nat their true boundary and encode outward values. Keep Effects lazy and flat;\nkeep one-use mapping and error logic beside the operation. Separate contracts,\nlive Layers, test Layers and application execution. Provider adapters expose\nnamed operations and immediately decode replies; no raw SDK client, generic\ncallback, `instanceof` policy or primitive secret configuration escapes.\nPublic service operations normally return a closed\n`Effect.Effect<Success, DomainError, never>`; dependencies are supplied when\ntheir Layer is built. Public effectful methods use named `Effect.fn`; private\nwork stays in the caller's span unless it owns a separate external operation.\nInfer types from one owning Schema and reuse whole-record checks as well as\nfields/brands. Do not re-decode checked internal values, mirror primitive\nrefinements or JSON-encode internal cache keys. New constrained values use the\nowner's fallible constructor with named failures. Convert semantic absence to\nOption while preserving any historical missing/null encoding and source hashes\nat their actual codec boundary.\n\nCooper requires a stronger functional policy than the skill's minimum:\n\n- Bind owned values with `const`; no `let`/`var`, reassignment, increment/decrement,\n  property/index writes, deletion, mutable class fields or in-place updates.\n  This includes short-lived local builders and test observation arrays.\n- Domain and service values are readonly Schema-derived records, readonly\n  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9417},"formatted_output":"54:web check-types: src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx(132,33): error TS2375: Type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, undefined, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, undefined>' is not assignable to type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, ({ context, abortController, serverContext }: LoaderFnContext<Register, any, \"__root__\", {}, {}, ... 4 more ..., undefined>) => Promise<...>, ... 4 more ..., undefined>' with 'exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true'. Consider adding 'undefined' to the types of the target's properties.\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run changeset:status\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n        \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n        \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n        \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n        \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-schema-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-fallible-domain-values.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-parameter-table-relationships.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-core-ambient-type-portability.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-absence-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-request-absence.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-contract-closeout.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-shared-rate-admission.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-006\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n        \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n        \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n        \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n        \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n        \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n        \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n        \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n        \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n        \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n        \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n        \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run docs:validate\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n        \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n        \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n        \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n        \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n        \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\nomits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\nand writes ignored `.source/public-catalogue.json` only on success. No accepted\npages is a failure. Source acceptance is recorded independently for each page\nand navigation in the owner policy's exact bindings. Reviewed byte hashes\nprevent a later edit from silently inheriting acceptance. The docs-content\npackage build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\nbrowser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\nchecked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\nHTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\nprocessed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\nrefinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. The\nreplacement Website renders accepted pages using that private connection and\nbrowser-safe compiled presentation. Search interaction, discovery and old-app\nretirement remain T005 work.\n\n`docs/architecture`\n: Durable implementation architecture.\n\n`docs/product-specs`\n: Current product/spec intent for repo development.\n\n## Public docs graph\n\n```ts\nProduction: public docs request\n\nbrowser\n  -> apps/docs route\n    -> apps/docs route boundary schema\n    -> DocsContentService\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\ninterruption/scopes release resources.\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:1454:### Native Website documentation qualification\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:378:This does not yet connect Website documentation loaders or replace its routes.\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:382:## Replacement Website documentation composition\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:385:four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations. One server\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:420:reading without JavaScript. Search and discovery are later T005 work. The\n`CALCULATOR_RATE_NAMESPACE` is a required positive decimal string selected by\nthe operator for that account and stage. No cloud value is invented. The guarded\ndisposable development root explicitly selects `local-emulator`, one shared\nloopback allowance and its isolated local namespace. Hosted composition defaults\nto `edge`; the local allowance additionally requires an HTTP loopback API origin.\nMissing hosted identity still fails safely. The native RPC does not transfer an\nexplicit AbortSignal on the pinned runtime: client cancellation stops local\nwaiting, while the existing API operation budget bounds remote work. No\nexperimental platform flag or dependency upgrade is introduced.\n\n\nKeep owning Schemas, schema-derived types, branded identities, checked semantic\nConfig, services, Layers and tagged errors. Core ledger types now infer from their Schema;\nrecursive trace types share one field owner and annotate only children. Existing\nencoded bytes, field order and omission/undefined behaviour stay unchanged.\nThis type-owner slice does not complete the remaining fallible constructors,\nsemantic Option migration or table relationship checks. Decode unknown representations once\nat their true boundary and encode outward values. Keep Effects lazy and flat;\nkeep one-use mapping and error logic beside the operation. Separate contracts,\nlive Layers, test Layers and application execution. Provider adapters expose\nnamed operations and immediately decode replies; no raw SDK client, generic\ncallback, `instanceof` policy or primitive secret configuration escapes.\nPublic service operations normally return a closed\n`Effect.Effect<Success, DomainError, never>`; dependencies are supplied when\ntheir Layer is built. Public effectful methods use named `Effect.fn`; private\nwork stays in the caller's span unless it owns a separate external operation.\nInfer types from one owning Schema and reuse whole-record checks as well as\nfields/brands. Do not re-decode checked internal values, mirror primitive\nrefinements or JSON-encode internal cache keys. New constrained values use the\nowner's fallible constructor with named failures. Convert semantic absence to\nOption while preserving any historical missing/null encoding and source hashes\nat their actual codec boundary.\n\nCooper requires a stronger functional policy than the skill's minimum:\n\n- Bind owned values with `const`; no `let`/`var`, reassignment, increment/decrement,\n  property/index writes, deletion, mutable class fields or in-place updates.\n  This includes short-lived local builders and test observation arrays.\n- Domain and service values are readonly Schema-derived records, readonly\n  bounded arrays or persistent Effect collections. Do not expose a mutable\n  array, native Map/Set/WeakMap/WeakSet, Date, SDK object or mutable reference as\n  a domain value.\n  Do not use casts or shallow freezing as a substitute for this contract.\n- Express transformations with pure Effect collection mapping/folding;\n  express workflows with named Effects and combinators. No `for`, `for...in`,\n  `for...of`, `while`, `do...while` or native array traversal, including native\n  `forEach`, in owned code. Pure array work uses Effect Array functions directly;\n  use scoped, bounded Effect traversal/repetition where work really repeats.\n- Prefer a pipe for a clear linear data flow. Use flat `Effect.gen` with\n  immutable bindings when dependencies or several sequential steps make that\n  clearer. Neither syntax permits raw work, mutation, hidden branching or\n  helper chains that obscure the operation.\n- Expected failures stay in tagged error channels and are handled exhaustively\n  with Effect/Match and Option/Result's matching APIs. No `switch`, manual\n  `_tag` comparisons, thrown expected errors, `try`/`catch`, manual Promise\n  control flow, manual unknown probing or nullable domain state.\n- Pure deterministic calculations and rendering remain total plain functions.\n  Do not wrap constants or safe leaf transformations in ceremonial Effects,\n  or construct a service/Layer for every helper.\n\nNecessary changing state belongs to the narrowest explicit owner: React for\nlocal synchronous input/display state; Effect Atom for browser work; or scoped\nRef/Queue/Cache/Semaphore/transaction facilities inside a named Layer where\ntheir semantics are needed. Values held in those owners remain immutable;\nupdates are pure and atomic, and no underlying mutable reference escapes.\nThere is no claim that React, Effect, the host or a vendor SDK has no internal\nstate. Prove route/request/instance lifetime, concurrent updates, interruption\nand disposal rather than hiding state in module globals. Calculation facts and\nreports get no persistence or cache; accepted public content may have an\nexplicit bounded cache policy.\n\n"},"started_at_ms":1791307972957,"completed_at_ms":1791307972957}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T17:32:53.011Z","ordinal":49337,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11246-8193-7c42-b239-24586ac4bd83","call_id":"call_GevvUTW4iTB432oSLh9SPvMF","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5186)\nTotal output lines: 254\n\n54:web check-types: src/lib/health-loader.boundary.browser.test.tsx(132,33): error TS2375: Type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, undefined, unknown, unknown, unknown, unknown, undefined>' is not assignable to type 'RootRoute<Register, undefined, RouterContext, AnyContext, AnyContext, {}, ({ context, abortController, serverContext }: LoaderFnContext<Register, any, \"__root__\", {}, {}, ... 4 more ..., undefined>) => Promise<...>, ... 4 more ..., undefined>' with 'exactOptionalPropertyTypes: true'. Consider adding 'undefined' to the types of the target's properties.\n        \"bun run test\",\n        \"bun run changeset:status\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Exercise each supported calculator with representative valid and invalid values, all states, keyboard/focus and accessible result announcements.\",\n        \"Check latest-input-wins, cancelled calculations, navigation/unmount cleanup, no saved figures and no figures in URL/history/share metadata.\",\n        \"Prove explicit Calculate, stale-answer indication and cancellation on edits, accessible expandable breakdown/assumptions/sources and supported-year visibility, without exporting input or trace values to telemetry.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call graph, package/export direction, canonical Schemas/types/brands/errors/Config, live/test/runtime separation and boundary decode/encode.\",\n        \"Inspect mutation/reassignment/loops/native mutators, readonly values, unsafe casts, raw provider/client escapes, nested runtimes and helper/module purpose. Verify actual-command rejected and accepted fixtures at the actual paths; exact host exceptions cannot silently disable other policy.\",\n        \"Check applicable route/container/leaf composition, browser-safe imports, interruption/resource disposal and bounded safe telemetry.\",\n        \"Apply the SPEC's path-evidenced downstream-impact rows to this slice; required docs/README/skill/lint/config/CI/runbook changes cannot be deferred to closeout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"Every existing calculator is usable and returns the retained result for the same valid inputs.\",\n        \"Unsupported years and expected failures have checked visible outcomes; UI copy does not imply wider tax support.\",\n        \"Packed consumers use only public exports and dispose the new caller-owned client; fresh interfaces are versioned deliberately.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-04-sdk-client-lifetime.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-schema-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-fallible-domain-values.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-parameter-table-relationships.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-core-ambient-type-portability.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-absence-owners.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-public-request-absence.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-domain-contract-closeout.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-shared-rate-admission.json\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"CSF-T005\",\n      \"title\": \"Replace public docs and all discovery representations\",\n      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n      \"type\": \"vertical-slice\",\n      \"acceptedFindingIds\": [],\n      \"requirementIds\": [\n        \"CSF-006\",\n        \"CSF-010\"\n      ],\n      \"dependsOn\": [\n        \"CSF-T003\",\n        \"CSF-T004\"\n      ],\n      \"goal\": \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n      \"scope\": [\n        \"Review the retained authored pages and navigation for finished content and source fidelity, recording exact publication acceptance and excluding unfinished drafts from public search.\",\n        \"Implement one accepted content/page catalogue. Website owns HTML and browser-safe generated presentation exports; dynamic page/navigation/source/search/Markdown/image services belong to the backend and checked client contract. Generated static sitemap/robots/agent indexes/Markdown/OG assets need no extra API.\",\n        \"Generate useful deterministic 1200x630 page OG images from checked public page metadata with the selected current Takumi/font graph; never incorporate calculation values.\",\n        \"Retire apps/docs and replaced rendering/build paths once equivalent local journeys and retained source/artifact identities are proved; update current owners and preserve addressability of history/old useful URLs.\",\n        \"Replace hard-coded apps/docs browser/cache/quality paths in tools/quality-workflow/** and .github/workflows/quality.yml; update the docs browser command in packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and current owners in docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json.\",\n        \"Apply Q13: processed Markdown exposes only accepted public pages/reference content. Personal report downloads are outside this release; calculation answers remain temporary and visible on screen or through the agreed agent tools. Any public-content cache uses an owned readonly structured key with installed Equal/Hash semantics, not JSON; prove equivalent reconstructed keys, distinct address fields and last-reader cancellation cleanup where a shared cache is needed.\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"packages/content/** compiled canonical page/navigation/errors and accepted catalogue service; docs-content preserves compatibility re-exports.\",\n        \"packages/docs-content/** authored/status/navigation/generated owners and any justified retained docs-fumadocs bridge\",\n        \"packages/docs-examples/** checked source/compiler/runtime owner; preserve the four retained integration templates and their output/error expectations.\",\n        \"apps/web HTML/docs presentation, generated static discovery/image assets and old-route redirect map\",\n        \"apps/api dynamic page/navigation/search/processed-Markdown/image services and packages/api/http checked contracts/clients; owning content package preserves prose, links, tables and examples\",\n        \"tools/documentation/owner-policy.json exact public acceptance records and generated edges\",\n        \"Public/app/package READMEs, docs/architecture/frontend.md, content-and-posts.md, package-ownership.md and applicable runbook/command pointers\",\n        \"tools/quality-workflow/**, .github/workflows/quality.yml, package.json/Turbo command wiring, packages/scripts/src/release-readiness/schemas.ts and docs/verification/repository-harness-profile.json\"\n      ],\n      \"implementationPrompt\": \"Read the proposed/accepted SPEC and its current/target/test call graphs before editing. Implement only this named slice after final shared understanding and its task prerequisites are settled. Use immutable canonical Schema-derived values, brands/errors/Config, closed named services, separate live/test Layers and application-owned execution. Keep lazy flat Effects and pipes where linear data flow is clearer; no local mutation, imperative loops, helper sprawl or generic callbacks. Necessary changing state has an explicit React/Effect owner and pure updates. Exact host exceptions admit only their required construct. Change owning docs, READMEs, exports, enforcement and operational pointers in the same slice. Report any design mismatch and update the SPEC/tasks before acceptance. Use bounded independent factual research/review only where authorised and justified.\",\n      \"mandatoryVerification\": [\n        \"bun run docs:validate\",\n        \"bun run check:docs\",\n        \"bun run check:runbooks\",\n        \"bun run build\",\n        \"bun run check-types\",\n        \"bun run verification\",\n        \"Appropriate Changeset for package-facing work; explicit no-Changeset rationale otherwise.\"\n      ],\n      \"browserVerification\": [\n        \"Verify public docs/navigation, search, Markdown negotiation/explicit links, crawler-readable rendering, canonicals and share previews on actual local routes.\",\n        \"Check draft exclusion, no raw JSX/imports in processed Markdown, valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.\"\n      ],\n      \"qualityAudits\": [\n        \"Review this slice's actual call…186 tokens truncated…oseout.\"\n      ],\n      \"parentAudit\": {\n        \"required\": true,\n        \"basis\": \"Primary owner reviews the diff, named outcomes, focused and complete checks, applicable real journeys, source evidence and affected owner/pointer changes.\",\n        \"recovery\": \"Correct or re-scope a proved defect. Seek a decision only for a material unresolved product choice or consequential operation without authority; keep incomplete proof identifiable.\"\n      },\n      \"completionCriteria\": [\n        \"All representations use the same accepted catalogue; no parallel hand-maintained index or fake published status exists.\",\n        \"The Website imports only browser-safe compiled presentation/contract exports; dynamic content machine routes and authored source/live Layers belong to the backend.\",\n        \"Quality/cache/release/profile owners admit the replacement app and no longer depend on a removed apps/docs path; new commands exist and are proved before obsolete commands are removed.\",\n        \"Finished pages are explicitly accepted, unfinished pages do not enter public discovery, and valid public content retains source attribution.\",\n        \"The replacement covers the retired app's useful journeys and historical evidence remains addressable.\"\n      ],\n      \"commitAfterPassing\": true,\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-checked-docs-source-owner.json\",\nomits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\nand writes ignored `.source/public-catalogue.json` only on success. No accepted\npages is a failure. Source acceptance is recorded independently for each page\nand navigation in the owner policy's exact bindings. Reviewed byte hashes\nprevent a later edit from silently inheriting acceptance. The docs-content\npackage build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\nbrowser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\nchecked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\nHTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\nprocessed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\nrefinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. The\nreplacement Website renders accepted pages using that private connection and\nbrowser-safe compiled presentation. Search interaction, discovery and old-app\nretirement remain T005 work.\n\n`docs/architecture`\n: Durable implementation architecture.\n\n`docs/product-specs`\n: Current product/spec intent for repo development.\n\n## Public docs graph\n\n```ts\nProduction: public docs request\n\nbrowser\n  -> apps/docs route\n    -> apps/docs route boundary schema\n    -> DocsContentService\n\nUse [the repo-owned effect client wrapper skill](../../.agents/skills/effect-client-wrapper/SKILL.md)\nwhen introducing or reviewing a provider adapter. Its canonical example and\nstale-pattern audit are acceptance requirements, not an optional template.\n\n## Runtime composition\n\nUse `ManagedRuntime.make(...)` for module-scoped app runtimes that run many\nEffects against the same fully provided service graph. Do not create a\n`ManagedRuntime` inside route loaders, React components, request handlers or\nper-operation helpers. The docs app owns one server-only managed runtime and an\nexplicit disposal operation for focused tests and host lifecycle integration;\nit has no browser Effect runtime. Browser routes restore the schema-encoded\nserver-function transport and render canonical values.\n\nThe Website candidate owns one server runner and a React Atom registry in the\nbrowser. Its typed route context contains named framework settings/catalogue and\ndocumentation page transports, never an Effect runtime or Context. The root restores encoded values and passes\nchecked submission state through ordinary React context. The container owns\ncommands; focused leaves render readonly values. Editing and form unmount\ninterrupt active work. Private binding transport belongs to the server Layer;\npublic browser transport belongs to the registry. The RPC protocol Layer keeps\nconfiguration, while each named native client receive loop has an operation scope.\nNo calculation or catalogue read builds a Layer or runner. See the [Website owner](../../apps/web/README.md).\nThe SDK owns one runtime per client, with caller disposal and bounded one-shot\nhelpers; see the [SDK lifetime owner](api-and-sdk.md#typescript-sdk-facade).\n\nUse `@effect/platform-bun/BunRuntime.runMain(...)` for Bun process entrypoints\nwhere the root Effect is the process lifecycle. Process entrypoints should\ncompose config, platform layers and server layers, then let Effect\ninterruption/scopes release resources.\ndocs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md:1454:### Native Website documentation qualification\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:378:This does not yet connect Website documentation loaders or replace its routes.\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:382:## Replacement Website documentation composition\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:385:four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations. One server\ndocs/architecture/frontend.md:420:reading without JavaS