dd a narrow content-owned public-discovery contract for sitemap, robots and the short/full agent indexes. A single named backend service captures the accepted catalogue and a semantic checked Website origin. It derives each bounded document from those immutable values. The API supplies its actual checked configuration. HTTP and private named RPC expose the same service; the Website returns checked public documents at their conventional addresses. Search remains noindex. No calculation values, cache, collector or alternative source catalogue is introduced.\n\nBefore choosing the final API, inspect installed Effect HTTP text/content-type/HEAD/Accept helpers, the existing native bounded client and content configuration/type ownership. Reuse one semantic origin Schema instead of copying primitive validation or creating an API/content dependency cycle. Keep native caller cancellation and expected errors checked. A generated static asset can use the same projection later if actual origin/configuration is available at its owning build boundary; do not bake fixture or guessed Production addresses.\n\nExisting scope still requires processed Markdown negotiation, page share images and app retirement. Preserve old useful page addresses and retain authored content/review/navigation/templates. The isolated Takumi probe qualified native/Wasm parity for all 61 public metadata rows, but no renderer/dependency/image route is in the repository yet. Its proof cannot stand in for the actual final app.\n\nRequired local oracles: actual built API and Website responses, correct media types, complete catalogue coverage and exact configured canonical origin, escaped XML/text, draft exclusion, robots/search policy, real agent index links and content, no raw MDX/JSX/import source, explicit Markdown links plus Accept negotiation, safe unavailable/malformed/version replies, GET/HEAD semantics where adopted, retained calculator/private-content restrictions and all current journeys. Update durabl