{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:12:22.901Z","ordinal":50061,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f188b3f1-1e20-4159-9817-cb7ccadc045c","process_id":"51812","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md","name":"repository-profile.md","path":".agents/skills/package-structure/references/repository-profile.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# TaxKit package profile\n\n- Repository root: current checkout resolved with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Package manager/workspaces: Bun with the root's nested workspace globs\n- Namespace: `@taxkit/*`\n- Source condition: `source`\n- Default internal build: `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`\n- Exceptions: `@taxkit/docs-content` and private `@taxkit/infrastructure` are source-only; `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` is private compiled; the TypeScript SDK is publishable/dist-only and requires clean publish exports, packed-artifact, and downstream-consumer proof\n- Changesets and production Knip are part of release-facing package changes\n- Verification: focused package commands, `bun run test:skills`, and `bun run verification`; for release-facing work run `bun run release:check` (including SDK packed/downstream checks)\n- Architecture routes: `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`, `docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`, and `docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`\n- Preserve unrelated work; never overwrite it.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# TaxKit package profile\n\n- Repository root: current checkout resolved with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Package manager/workspaces: Bun with the root's nested workspace globs\n- Namespace: `@taxkit/*`\n- Source condition: `source`\n- Default internal build: `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`\n- Exceptions: `@taxkit/docs-content` and private `@taxkit/infrastructure` are source-only; `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` is private compiled; the TypeScript SDK is publishable/dist-only and requires clean publish exports, packed-artifact, and downstream-consumer proof\n- Changesets and production Knip are part of release-facing package changes\n- Verification: focused package commands, `bun run test:skills`, and `bun run verification`; for release-facing work run `bun run release:check` (including SDK packed/downstream checks)\n- Architecture routes: `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`, `docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`, and `docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`\n- Preserve unrelated work; never overwrite it.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":23667},"formatted_output":"# TaxKit package profile\n\n- Repository root: current checkout resolved with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\n- Package manager/workspaces: Bun with the root's nested workspace globs\n- Namespace: `@taxkit/*`\n- Source condition: `source`\n- Default internal build: `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`\n- Exceptions: `@taxkit/docs-content` and private `@taxkit/infrastructure` are source-only; `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` is private compiled; the TypeScript SDK is publishable/dist-only and requires clean publish exports, packed-artifact, and downstream-consumer proof\n- Changesets and production Knip are part of release-facing package changes\n- Verification: focused package commands, `bun run test:skills`, and `bun run verification`; for release-facing work run `bun run release:check` (including SDK packed/downstream checks)\n- Architecture routes: `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`, `docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`, and `docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`\n- Preserve unrelated work; never overwrite it.\n\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\n\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\n\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791310342899,"completed_at_ms":1791310342901}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:12:22.902Z","ordinal":50062,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-492d3cf3-8644-4c77-93ba-e683ec592036","process_id":"11462","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat packages/content/src/test.layer.ts"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat packages/content/src/test.layer.ts","name":"test.layer.ts","path":"packages/content/src/test.layer.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"import { Array, Effect, Layer, Ref } from \"effect\";\n\nimport type { ContentObservations } from \"./__testing__/observations.js\";\nimport { ContentServiceLive } from \"./live.layer.js\";\nimport type {\n  DocsPagePath,\n  DocsPublicCatalogue,\n  DocsSearchTerm,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { ContentCatalogue, ContentService } from \"./service.js\";\n\nexport const makeContentTest = Effect.fnUntraced(function* (\n  catalogue: DocsPublicCatalogue\n) {\n  const service = yield* ContentService.pipe(\n    Effect.provide(\n      ContentServiceLive.pipe(\n        Layer.provide(Layer.succeed(ContentCatalogue, catalogue))\n      )\n    )\n  );\n  const observations = {\n    requestedPages: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsPagePath[]>([]),\n    searchTerms: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsSearchTerm[]>([]),\n  } satisfies ContentObservations;\n  return {\n    layer: Layer.succeed(\n      ContentService,\n      ContentService.of({\n        getNavigation: service.getNavigation,\n        getPage: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.getPage\")(function* (\n          path: DocsPagePath\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.requestedPages, Array.append(path));\n          return yield* service.getPage(path);\n        }),\n        listPages: service.listPages,\n        searchPages: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.searchPages\")(function* (\n          term: DocsSearchTerm\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.searchTerms, Array.append(term));\n          return yield* service.searchPages(term);\n        }),\n      })\n    ),\n    observations,\n  };\n});\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"import { Array, Effect, Layer, Ref } from \"effect\";\n\nimport type { ContentObservations } from \"./__testing__/observations.js\";\nimport { ContentServiceLive } from \"./live.layer.js\";\nimport type {\n  DocsPagePath,\n  DocsPublicCatalogue,\n  DocsSearchTerm,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { ContentCatalogue, ContentService } from \"./service.js\";\n\nexport const makeContentTest = Effect.fnUntraced(function* (\n  catalogue: DocsPublicCatalogue\n) {\n  const service = yield* ContentService.pipe(\n    Effect.provide(\n      ContentServiceLive.pipe(\n        Layer.provide(Layer.succeed(ContentCatalogue, catalogue))\n      )\n    )\n  );\n  const observations = {\n    requestedPages: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsPagePath[]>([]),\n    searchTerms: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsSearchTerm[]>([]),\n  } satisfies ContentObservations;\n  return {\n    layer: Layer.succeed(\n      ContentService,\n      ContentService.of({\n        getNavigation: service.getNavigation,\n        getPage: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.getPage\")(function* (\n          path: DocsPagePath\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.requestedPages, Array.append(path));\n          return yield* service.getPage(path);\n        }),\n        listPages: service.listPages,\n        searchPages: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.searchPages\")(function* (\n          term: DocsSearchTerm\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.searchTerms, Array.append(term));\n          return yield* service.searchPages(term);\n        }),\n      })\n    ),\n    observations,\n  };\n});\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8500},"formatted_output":"import { Array, Effect, Layer, Ref } from \"effect\";\n\nimport type { ContentObservations } from \"./__testing__/observations.js\";\nimport { ContentServiceLive } from \"./live.layer.js\";\nimport type {\n  DocsPagePath,\n  DocsPublicCatalogue,\n  DocsSearchTerm,\n} from \"./schemas.js\";\nimport { ContentCatalogue, ContentService } from \"./service.js\";\n\nexport const makeContentTest = Effect.fnUntraced(function* (\n  catalogue: DocsPublicCatalogue\n) {\n  const service = yield* ContentService.pipe(\n    Effect.provide(\n      ContentServiceLive.pipe(\n        Layer.provide(Layer.succeed(ContentCatalogue, catalogue))\n      )\n    )\n  );\n  const observations = {\n    requestedPages: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsPagePath[]>([]),\n    searchTerms: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsSearchTerm[]>([]),\n  } satisfies ContentObservations;\n  return {\n    layer: Layer.succeed(\n      ContentService,\n      ContentService.of({\n        getNavigation: service.getNavigation,\n        getPage: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.getPage\")(function* (\n          path: DocsPagePath\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.requestedPages, Array.append(path));\n          return yield* service.getPage(path);\n        }),\n        listPages: service.listPages,\n        searchPages: Effect.fn(\"ContentService.searchPages\")(function* (\n          term: DocsSearchTerm\n        ) {\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.searchTerms, Array.append(term));\n          return yield* service.searchPages(term);\n        }),\n      })\n    ),\n    observations,\n  };\n});\n"},"started_at_ms":1791310342899,"completed_at_ms":1791310342901}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:12:22.903Z","ordinal":50063,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-69a4a184-006d-454a-adf5-310f33dada77","process_id":"56569","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat .agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md","name":"package-contract.md","path":".agents/skills/package-structure/references/package-contract.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Package contract\n\n## Ownership before files\n\nName the capability, its callers, its untrusted boundaries, its runtime owner,\nand why an existing package cannot own it. A package is justified by a stable\nsemantic boundary, not by file count.\n\nCompiled packages use `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, relative internal imports\nwith explicit `.js` endings, and explicit exports. Use the same endings in\ntests; TypeScript and the source consumer resolve them to the matching `.ts`\nfiles, while ordinary ESM consumers load the emitted `.js` files. Root exports\nare absent by default; an intentional root\nmust remain contract-only. The source condition maps to `src`, `types` to\ndeclarations, and `default` to `dist`. `publishConfig.exports` omits the source\ncondition. Source-only packages point both development/default resolution at\nsource and explain the bundler requirement in their package README.\n\nRequired Effect service paths:\n\n```text\nsrc/schemas.ts\nsrc/errors.ts\nsrc/service.ts\nsrc/live.layer.ts\nsrc/test.layer.ts\nsrc/__testing__/fixtures.ts\nsrc/__testing__/observations.ts\ntest/service.test.ts\n```\n\nUse `mock.layer.ts` only when its semantics are distinct from the deterministic\ntest Layer. Tests live under `test/`; `src/__testing__` contains reusable setup,\nfixtures, and observations only.\n\nEach package README names the semantic owner, public/live/test export paths,\ndownstream architecture/proof impact, runbook applicability, and explicit\nnon-claims. Repository profiles—not this global contract—name exact local\ncommands and document paths.\n\n## Separate source, domain and transport owners\n\nAuthored content may live in a source-only package. It exports files and source\ninventory; the domain package owns the validation Schemas and source loader,\nservice, named errors and live/test Layers. Apps supply bundler/host adapters.\nDo not give the source package another runtime or duplicate domain definitions.\nHTTP, RPC and MCP reuse explicit domain exports. Client exports must resolve\nwithout importing handlers, the live source loader, renderer or MCP server.\nCheck the actual browser bundle as well as the export map.\n\n## Export proof\n\nConsumer fixtures must prove all four modes:\n\n1. repository source condition resolves source;\n2. TypeScript resolves emitted declarations;\n3. default resolution uses built JavaScript;\n4. packed/publish exports omit source-only paths and conditions.\n\nNever rely only on checking that export keys exist.\n\n`publishConfig.exports` is not a portable manifest rewrite: npm and Bun pack may\nretain the development `exports` map, while other package managers may apply the\npublish map. A publishable package therefore needs the repository's explicit\nstaged-manifest/prepack path and tarball inspection. Prove the actual publisher\nused by that repository; do not infer a clean tarball from `publishConfig`.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Package contract\n\n## Ownership before files\n\nName the capability, its callers, its untrusted boundaries, its runtime owner,\nand why an existing package cannot own it. A package is justified by a stable\nsemantic boundary, not by file count.\n\nCompiled packages use `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, relative internal imports\nwith explicit `.js` endings, and explicit exports. Use the same endings in\ntests; TypeScript and the source consumer resolve them to the matching `.ts`\nfiles, while ordinary ESM consumers load the emitted `.js` files. Root exports\nare absent by default; an intentional root\nmust remain contract-only. The source condition maps to `src`, `types` to\ndeclarations, and `default` to `dist`. `publishConfig.exports` omits the source\ncondition. Source-only packages point both development/default resolution at\nsource and explain the bundler requirement in their package README.\n\nRequired Effect service paths:\n\n```text\nsrc/schemas.ts\nsrc/errors.ts\nsrc/service.ts\nsrc/live.layer.ts\nsrc/test.layer.ts\nsrc/__testing__/fixtures.ts\nsrc/__testing__/observations.ts\ntest/service.test.ts\n```\n\nUse `mock.layer.ts` only when its semantics are distinct from the deterministic\ntest Layer. Tests live under `test/`; `src/__testing__` contains reusable setup,\nfixtures, and observations only.\n\nEach package README names the semantic owner, public/live/test export paths,\ndownstream architecture/proof impact, runbook applicability, and explicit\nnon-claims. Repository profiles—not this global contract—name exact local\ncommands and document paths.\n\n## Separate source, domain and transport owners\n\nAuthored content may live in a source-only package. It exports files and source\ninventory; the domain package owns the validation Schemas and source loader,\nservice, named errors and live/test Layers. Apps supply bundler/host adapters.\nDo not give the source package another runtime or duplicate domain definitions.\nHTTP, RPC and MCP reuse explicit domain exports. Client exports must resolve\nwithout importing handlers, the live source loader, renderer or MCP server.\nCheck the actual browser bundle as well as the export map.\n\n## Export proof\n\nConsumer fixtures must prove all four modes:\n\n1. repository source condition resolves source;\n2. TypeScript resolves emitted declarations;\n3. default resolution uses built JavaScript;\n4. packed/publish exports omit source-only paths and conditions.\n\nNever rely only on checking that export keys exist.\n\n`publishConfig.exports` is not a portable manifest rewrite: npm and Bun pack may\nretain the development `exports` map, while other package managers may apply the\npublish map. A publishable package therefore needs the repository's explicit\nstaged-manifest/prepack path and tarball inspection. Prove the actual publisher\nused by that repository; do not infer a clean tarball from `publishConfig`.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7917},"formatted_output":"# Package contract\n\n## Ownership before files\n\nName the capability, its callers, its untrusted boundaries, its runtime owner,\nand why an existing package cannot own it. A package is justified by a stable\nsemantic boundary, not by file count.\n\nCompiled packages use `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, relative internal imports\nwith explicit `.js` endings, and explicit exports. Use the same endings in\ntests; TypeScript and the source consumer resolve them to the matching `.ts`\nfiles, while ordinary ESM consumers load the emitted `.js` files. Root exports\nare absent by default; an intentional root\nmust remain contract-only. The source condition maps to `src`, `types` to\ndeclarations, and `default` to `dist`. `publishConfig.exports` omits the source\ncondition. Source-only packages point both development/default resolution at\nsource and explain the bundler requirement in their package README.\n\nRequired Effect service paths:\n\n```text\nsrc/schemas.ts\nsrc/errors.ts\nsrc/service.ts\nsrc/live.layer.ts\nsrc/test.layer.ts\nsrc/__testing__/fixtures.ts\nsrc/__testing__/observations.ts\ntest/service.test.ts\n```\n\nUse `mock.layer.ts` only when its semantics are distinct from the deterministic\ntest Layer. Tests live under `test/`; `src/__testing__` contains reusable setup,\nfixtures, and observations only.\n\nEach package README names the semantic owner, public/live/test export paths,\ndownstream architecture/proof impact, runbook applicability, and explicit\nnon-claims. Repository profiles—not this global contract—name exact local\ncommands and document paths.\n\n## Separate source, domain and transport owners\n\nAuthored content may live in a source-only package. It exports files and source\ninventory; the domain package owns the validation Schemas and source loader,\nservice, named errors and live/test Layers. Apps supply bundler/host adapters.\nDo not give the source package another runtime or duplicate domain definitions.\nHTTP, RPC and MCP reuse explicit domain exports. Client exports must resolve\nwithout importing handlers, the live source loader, renderer or MCP server.\nCheck the actual browser bundle as well as the export map.\n\n## Export proof\n\nConsumer fixtures must prove all four modes:\n\n1. repository source condition resolves source;\n2. TypeScript resolves emitted declarations;\n3. default resolution uses built JavaScript;\n4. packed/publish exports omit source-only paths and conditions.\n\nNever rely only on checking that export keys exist.\n\n`publishConfig.exports` is not a portable manifest rewrite: npm and Bun pack may\nretain the development `exports` map, while other package managers may apply the\npublish map. A publishable package therefore needs the repository's explicit\nstaged-manifest/prepack path and tarball inspection. Prove the actual publisher\nused by that repository; do not infer a clean tarball from `publishConfig`.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791310342899,"completed_at_ms":1791310342901}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:12:22.967Z","ordinal":50064,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1126a-ab37-7e01-b8ba-535a52154f1a","call_id":"call_4e57301c2b7c4f868ab424aa605ed98c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"4d6c2d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000425,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":361,\"output\":\"import { Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nimport {\\n  DocsNonEmptyText,\\n  DocsPagePath,\\n  DocsPageSlug,\\n  DocsSourcePath,\\n} from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\n\\nexport const DocsSourceOperation = Schema.Literals([\\n  \\\"decode\\\",\\n  \\\"getNavigation\\\",\\n  \\\"getPage\\\",\\n  \\\"listPages\\\",\\n  \\\"read\\\",\\n  \\\"searchPages\\\",\\n  \\\"validateContent\\\",\\n]);\\nexport type DocsSourceOperation = typeof DocsSourceOperation.Type;\\n\\n// Public transports share these fixed failures; internal source errors retain\\n// their checked diagnostic fields only inside the content application.\\nexport class DocsPageUnavailable extends Schema.TaggedError<DocsPageUnavailable>()(\\n  \\\"DocsPageUnavailable\\\",\\n  { message: Schema.Literal(\\\"The documentation page was not found.\\\") }\\n) {}\\n\\nexport class DocsSearchUnavailable extends Schema.TaggedError<DocsSearchUnavailable>()(\\n  \\\"DocsSearchUnavailable\\\",\\n  {\\n    message: Schema.Literal(\\\"Documentation search is temporarily unavailable.\\\"),\\n  }\\n) {}\\n\\nexport class DocsPageNotFoundError extends Schema.TaggedError<DocsPageNotFoundError>()(\\n  \\\"DocsPageNotFoundError\\\",\\n  {\\n    path: DocsPagePath,\\n  }\\n) {}\\n\\nexport class DocsSlugNotFoundError extends Schema.TaggedError<DocsSlugNotFoundError>()(\\n  \\\"DocsSlugNotFoundError\\\",\\n  {\\n    slug: DocsPageSlug,\\n  }\\n) {}\\n\\nexport class DocsSourceError extends Schema.TaggedError<DocsSourceError>()(\\n  \\\"DocsSourceError\\\",\\n  {\\n    message: DocsNonEmptyText,\\n    operation: DocsSourceOperation,\\n    source: Schema.optional(DocsSourcePath),\\n  }\\n) {}\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"6f284e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.0000085,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":381,\"output\":\"import { Array, Effect, Layer, Ref } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nimport type { ContentObservations } from \\\"./__testing__/observations.js\\\";\\nimport { ContentServiceLive } from \\\"./live.layer.js\\\";\\nimport type {\\n  DocsPagePath,\\n  DocsPublicCatalogue,\\n  DocsSearchTerm,\\n} from \\\"./schemas.js\\\";\\nimport { ContentCatalogue, ContentService } from \\\"./service.js\\\";\\n\\nexport const makeContentTest = Effect.fnUntraced(function* (\\n  catalogue: DocsPublicCatalogue\\n) {\\n  const service = yield* ContentService.pipe(\\n    Effect.provide(\\n      ContentServiceLive.pipe(\\n        Layer.provide(Layer.succeed(ContentCatalogue, catalogue))\\n      )\\n    )\\n  );\\n  const observations = {\\n    requestedPages: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsPagePath[]>([]),\\n    searchTerms: yield* Ref.make<readonly DocsSearchTerm[]>([]),\\n  } satisfies ContentObservations;\\n  return {\\n    layer: Layer.succeed(\\n      ContentService,\\n      ContentService.of({\\n        getNavigation: service.getNavigation,\\n        getPage: Effect.fn(\\\"ContentService.getPage\\\")(function* (\\n          path: DocsPagePath\\n        ) {\\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.requestedPages, Array.append(path));\\n          return yield* service.getPage(path);\\n        }),\\n        listPages: service.listPages,\\n        searchPages: Effect.fn(\\\"ContentService.searchPages\\\")(function* (\\n          term: DocsSearchTerm\\n        ) {\\n          yield* Ref.update(observations.searchTerms, Array.append(term));\\n          return yield* service.searchPages(term);\\n        }),\\n      })\\n    ),\\n    observations,\\n  };\\n});\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"1d03e6\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":90,\"output\":\"import { ContentServiceLive } from \\\"@taxkit/content/live\\\";\\nimport { ContentCatalogue } from \\\"@taxkit/content/service\\\";\\nimport { exampleContentCatalogue } from \\\"@taxkit/content/testing/fixtures\\\";\\nimport { Layer } from \\\"effect\\\";\\n\\nexport const ContentTestLive = ContentServiceLive.pipe(\\n  Layer.provide(Layer.effect(ContentCatalogue, exampleContentCatalogue))\\n);\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"b77c8d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.0000065,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":544,\"output\":\"import { DocsPublicPagePath, DocsSearchTerm } from \\\"@taxkit/content/schemas\\\";\\nimport { Effect, Result, Schema } from \\\"effect\\\";\\nimport type { RpcClient, RpcClientError } from \\\"effect/rpc\\\";\\n\\nimport type { DocsRpcGroup } from \\\"../src/content.group.js\\\";\\nimport type { DocsRpcClient } from \\\"../src/content.service.js\\\";\\n\\nexport const docsPath = Schema.decodeResult(DocsPublicPagePath)(\\n  \\\"/start/overview\\\"\\n).pipe(Result.getOrThrowWith(() => new Error(\\\"Invalid fixture page address\\\")));\\nexport const docsTerm = Schema.decodeResult(DocsSearchTerm)(\\\"Start\\\").pipe(\\n  Result.getOrThrowWith(() => new Error(\\\"Invalid fixture search term\\\"))\\n);\\nexport const DocsRpcOperationCases = [\\n  {\\n    invoke: (client: DocsRpcClient[\\\"Service\\\"]) =>\\n      client.getNavigation().pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    nativeInvoke: (\\n      client: RpcClient.FromGroup<\\n        typeof DocsRpcGroup,\\n        RpcClientError.RpcClientError\\n      >,\\n      version: string\\n    ) => client.GetDocsNavigation({ version }).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    operation: \\\"getNavigation\\\",\\n  },\\n  {\\n    invoke: (client: DocsRpcClient[\\\"Service\\\"]) =>\\n      client.getPage(docsPath).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    nativeInvoke: (\\n      client: RpcClient.FromGroup<\\n        typeof DocsRpcGroup,\\n        RpcClientError.RpcClientError\\n      >,\\n      version: string\\n    ) => client.GetDocsPage({ path: docsPath, version }).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    operation: \\\"getPage\\\",\\n  },\\n  {\\n    invoke: (client: DocsRpcClient[\\\"Service\\\"]) =>\\n      client.getMarkdown(docsPath).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    nativeInvoke: (\\n      client: RpcClient.FromGroup<\\n        typeof DocsRpcGroup,\\n        RpcClientError.RpcClientError\\n      >,\\n      version: string\\n    ) =>\\n      client.GetDocsMarkdown({ path: docsPath, version }).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    operation: \\\"getMarkdown\\\",\\n  },\\n  {\\n    invoke: (client: DocsRpcClient[\\\"Service\\\"]) =>\\n      client.searchPages(docsTerm).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    nativeInvoke: (\\n      client: RpcClient.FromGroup<\\n        typeof DocsRpcGroup,\\n        RpcClientError.RpcClientError\\n      >,\\n      version: string\\n    ) =>\\n      client.SearchDocsPages({ term: docsTerm, version }).pipe(Effect.asVoid),\\n    operation: \\\"searchPages\\\",\\n  },\\n];\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":4,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"c83c6b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000023667,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":495,\"output\":\"# TaxKit package profile\\n\\n- Repository root: current checkout resolved with `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`\\n- Package manager/workspaces: Bun with the root's nested workspace globs\\n- Namespace: `@taxkit/*`\\n- Source condition: `source`\\n- Default internal build: `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`\\n- Exceptions: `@taxkit/docs-content` and private `@taxkit/infrastructure` are source-only; `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs` is private compiled; the TypeScript SDK is publishable/dist-only and requires clean publish exports, packed-artifact, and downstream-consumer proof\\n- Changesets and production Knip are part of release-facing package changes\\n- Verification: focused package commands, `bun run test:skills`, and `bun run verification`; for release-facing work run `bun run release:check` (including SDK packed/downstream checks)\\n- Architecture routes: `docs/architecture/package-ownership.md`, `docs/architecture/package-boundaries.md`, `docs/architecture/effect-services.md`, and `docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md`\\n- Preserve unrelated work; never overwrite it.\\n\\n## Clean-slate compatibility and implementation\\n\\nThe local root manifest and lockfile select stable Effect 4.0.0 and TypeScript\\n7.0.2. Canonical skill templates may retain their upstream rc.117 qualification;\\nthat reference snapshot does not downgrade TaxKit or prove an app/provider\\nmigration. Check installed exports and the active clean-slate plan before use.\\n\\nThe complete local skill collection is pinned by\\n`tools/skills/canonical-skill-baseline.json` to Commonplace development-workflows\\n0.6.1. It includes `linear`, `strict-effect-ts` and `alchemy-iac`, with relative\\nClaude links. Use the Linear skill for tracked task status/evidence. The active\\n`docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md` distinguishes skill adoption, strict enforcement and Atom integration from\\nlater application work. Use its task receipts for current acceptance; the\\nupstream skill receipt alone does not prove runtime behaviour.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":5,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3d9893\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007917,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":712,\"output\":\"# Package contract\\n\\n## Ownership before files\\n\\nName the capability, its callers, its untrusted boundaries, its runtime owner,\\nand why an existing package cannot own it. A package is justified by a stable\\nsemantic boundary, not by file count.\\n\\nCompiled packages use `tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, relative internal imports\\nwith explicit `.js` endings, and explicit exports. Use the same endings in\\ntests; TypeScript and the source consumer resolve them to the matching `.ts`\\nfiles, while ordinary ESM consumers load the emitted `.js` files. Root exports\\nare absent by default; an intentional root\\nmust remain contract-only. The source condition maps to `src`, `types` to\\ndeclarations, and `default` to `dist`. `publishConfig.exports` omits the source\\ncondition. Source-only packages point both development/default resolution at\\nsource and explain the bundler requirement in their package README.\\n\\nRequired Effect service paths:\\n\\n```text\\nsrc/schemas.ts\\nsrc/errors.ts\\nsrc/service.ts\\nsrc/live.layer.ts\\nsrc/test.layer.ts\\nsrc/__testing__/fixtures.ts\\nsrc/__testing__/observations.ts\\ntest/service.test.ts\\n```\\n\\nUse `mock.layer.ts` only when its semantics are distinct from the deterministic\\ntest Layer. Tests live under `test/`; `src/__testing__` contains reusable setup,\\nfixtures, and observations only.\\n\\nEach package README names the semantic owner, public/live/test export paths,\\ndownstream architecture/proof impact, runbook applicability, and explicit\\nnon-claims. Repository profiles—not this global contract—name exact local\\ncommands and document paths.\\n\\n## Separate source, domain and transport owners\\n\\nAuthored content may live in a source-only package. It exports files and source\\ninventory; the domain package owns the validation Schemas and source loader,\\nservice, named errors and live/test Layers. Apps supply bundler/host adapters.\\nDo not give the source package another runtime or duplicate domain definitions.\\nHTTP, RPC and MCP reuse explicit domain exports. Client exports must resolve\\nwithout importing handlers, the live source loader, renderer or MCP server.\\nCheck the actual browser bundle as well as the export map.\\n\\n## Export proof\\n\\nConsumer fixtures must prove all four modes:\\n\\n1. repository source condition resolves source;\\n2. TypeScript resolves emitted declarations;\\n3. default resolution uses built JavaScript;\\n4. packed/publish exports omit source-only paths and conditions.\\n\\nNever rely only on checking that export keys exist.\\n\\n`publishConfig.exports` is not a portable manifest rewrite: npm and Bun pack may\\nretain the development `exports` map, while other package managers may apply the\\npublish map. A publishable package therefore needs the repository's explicit\\nstaged-manifest/prepack path and tarball inspection. Prove the actual publisher\\nused by that repository; do not infer a clean tarball from `publishConfig`.\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791310342.967041}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
