{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:28:12.967Z","ordinal":50412,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-328724c3-f37c-425b-bde2-220ca3e28a8d","process_id":"49394","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '198,230p' packages/api/rpc/README.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '198,230p' packages/api/rpc/README.md","name":"README.md","path":"packages/api/rpc/README.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\nRevision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\n\n## Documentation connection\n\n`./content/group`, `./content/schemas`, `./content/errors`, `./content/service`,\n`./content/handlers`, `./content/live` and `./content/test` own four named calls:\n`getNavigation`, `getPage`, `getMarkdown` and `searchPages`. Their native procedure\ntags are `GetDocsNavigation`, `GetDocsPage`, `GetDocsMarkdown` and `SearchDocsPages`.\nThe combined server group admits these alongside the existing nine calculator\nprocedures. Calculator clients and revision 4 stay unchanged; documentation\ncalls require their own revision 1 and fail with `DocsRpcVersionMismatch` during\nversion skew. There is no automatic retry or backend fallback.\n\n`DocsRpcClientLive` takes the existing checked API origin and caller-supplied\nHttpClient. Each call owns its native receive-loop scope, the ten-second whole\nreply deadline and the same private 2 MiB byte reader as calculator calls. That\nreader stops before an oversized tail, releases request/body resources and\nkeeps the native parser and response Schemas. Both clients map its private size\nmarker to their own fixed error. Request credentials, redirects and tracing\nuse the same qualified policy. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\n\nHandlers capture the supplied `ContentService` once and return its immutable\nvalues. Public missing-page and source-search errors use the content owner's\nfixed errors. The documentation procedure defect is a fixed literal; the native\nglobal fatal path retains its already qualified fixed literal. Internal source\ndiagnostics and raw Causes are not response values. The native API supplies the\nsame generated catalogue for HTTP and RPC. This package imports only compiled\ncontent contracts, with no MDX compiler or source collection dependency.\n\nFocused documentation tests cover all four calls, valid and incompatible\nversions, safe expected/global/procedure failures, damaged replies, unrelated\nadapter defects, exact/oversized encoded byte limits, headers/body deadlines,\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\nRevision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\n\n## Documentation connection\n\n`./content/group`, `./content/schemas`, `./content/errors`, `./content/service`,\n`./content/handlers`, `./content/live` and `./content/test` own four named calls:\n`getNavigation`, `getPage`, `getMarkdown` and `searchPages`. Their native procedure\ntags are `GetDocsNavigation`, `GetDocsPage`, `GetDocsMarkdown` and `SearchDocsPages`.\nThe combined server group admits these alongside the existing nine calculator\nprocedures. Calculator clients and revision 4 stay unchanged; documentation\ncalls require their own revision 1 and fail with `DocsRpcVersionMismatch` during\nversion skew. There is no automatic retry or backend fallback.\n\n`DocsRpcClientLive` takes the existing checked API origin and caller-supplied\nHttpClient. Each call owns its native receive-loop scope, the ten-second whole\nreply deadline and the same private 2 MiB byte reader as calculator calls. That\nreader stops before an oversized tail, releases request/body resources and\nkeeps the native parser and response Schemas. Both clients map its private size\nmarker to their own fixed error. Request credentials, redirects and tracing\nuse the same qualified policy. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\n\nHandlers capture the supplied `ContentService` once and return its immutable\nvalues. Public missing-page and source-search errors use the content owner's\nfixed errors. The documentation procedure defect is a fixed literal; the native\nglobal fatal path retains its already qualified fixed literal. Internal source\ndiagnostics and raw Causes are not response values. The native API supplies the\nsame generated catalogue for HTTP and RPC. This package imports only compiled\ncontent contracts, with no MDX compiler or source collection dependency.\n\nFocused documentation tests cover all four calls, valid and incompatible\nversions, safe expected/global/procedure failures, damaged replies, unrelated\nadapter defects, exact/oversized encoded byte limits, headers/body deadlines,\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5459},"formatted_output":"\nRevision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\n\n## Documentation connection\n\n`./content/group`, `./content/schemas`, `./content/errors`, `./content/service`,\n`./content/handlers`, `./content/live` and `./content/test` own four named calls:\n`getNavigation`, `getPage`, `getMarkdown` and `searchPages`. Their native procedure\ntags are `GetDocsNavigation`, `GetDocsPage`, `GetDocsMarkdown` and `SearchDocsPages`.\nThe combined server group admits these alongside the existing nine calculator\nprocedures. Calculator clients and revision 4 stay unchanged; documentation\ncalls require their own revision 1 and fail with `DocsRpcVersionMismatch` during\nversion skew. There is no automatic retry or backend fallback.\n\n`DocsRpcClientLive` takes the existing checked API origin and caller-supplied\nHttpClient. Each call owns its native receive-loop scope, the ten-second whole\nreply deadline and the same private 2 MiB byte reader as calculator calls. That\nreader stops before an oversized tail, releases request/body resources and\nkeeps the native parser and response Schemas. Both clients map its private size\nmarker to their own fixed error. Request credentials, redirects and tracing\nuse the same qualified policy. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\n\nHandlers capture the supplied `ContentService` once and return its immutable\nvalues. Public missing-page and source-search errors use the content owner's\nfixed errors. The documentation procedure defect is a fixed literal; the native\nglobal fatal path retains its already qualified fixed literal. Internal source\ndiagnostics and raw Causes are not response values. The native API supplies the\nsame generated catalogue for HTTP and RPC. This package imports only compiled\ncontent contracts, with no MDX compiler or source collection dependency.\n\nFocused documentation tests cover all four calls, valid and incompatible\nversions, safe expected/global/procedure failures, damaged replies, unrelated\nadapter defects, exact/oversized encoded byte limits, headers/body deadlines,\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311292965,"completed_at_ms":1791311292965}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:28:12.968Z","ordinal":50413,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3f850372-6dba-4030-9293-bb355280b106","process_id":"75196","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 55 docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 55 docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md","name":"content-and-posts.md","path":"docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\n```ts\nTests: docs structure\n\ndocs implementation\n  -> @taxkit/docs-content validate\n    -> frontmatter and navigation schema decode\n    -> navigation coverage and local link checks\n    -> MDX component allowlist\n    -> examples and OpenAPI reference checks\n  -> bun run check:docs\n  -> public/maintainer path separation and accepted status representation\n    -> generated Fumadocs and OpenAPI owner edges\n    -> maintainer metadata, links, commands and package README coverage\n  -> @taxkit/docs-fumadocs tests\n  -> apps/docs build and browser screenshots when rendering changes\n  -> bun run verification\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep public docs generic to callers and applications.\n- Do not document private downstream product strategy here.\n- Link to canonical architecture docs rather than duplicating them.\n- Treat old planning material as historical until revalidated.\n- Use [Documentation style](../standards/documentation-style.md) and the\n  related standards suite before writing or reviewing public docs.\n- Keep public MDX pages task-first. Use architecture docs for durable\n  ownership and runtime detail.\n- Validate public MDX through `@taxkit/docs-content`, which owns Effect Schema\n  frontmatter, navigation coverage, source-text policy, local link, MDX\n  component allowlist, examples and OpenAPI reference checks.\n- `draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate public\n  documentation; it is not accepted-current truth, publication, deployment,\n  external availability, correctness, or user visibility. `published` means\n  explicitly accepted current public documentation; it still does not establish\n  runtime or external availability. Preserve draft pages unless explicit\n  page-level acceptance records their transition.\n- Keep reusable Fumadocs code in `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs`; keep TaxKit\n  content contracts in `@taxkit/docs-content`; keep route composition and\n  app-specific rendering in `apps/docs`.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\n- [../product-specs/index.md](../product-specs/index.md)\n\n## Generated collection boundary\n\nGenerated collection adapters expose named Effect operations with safe tagged\nfailures. The collection owner wraps synchronous loader calls and processed-text\nPromise reads, preserving the SDK receiver. The reusable Fumadocs live Layer\ndecodes raw representations through its owning Schemas. Shiki metadata\ntransformation returns replacement nodes instead of mutating SDK-owned input.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\n```ts\nTests: docs structure\n\ndocs implementation\n  -> @taxkit/docs-content validate\n    -> frontmatter and navigation schema decode\n    -> navigation coverage and local link checks\n    -> MDX component allowlist\n    -> examples and OpenAPI reference checks\n  -> bun run check:docs\n  -> public/maintainer path separation and accepted status representation\n    -> generated Fumadocs and OpenAPI owner edges\n    -> maintainer metadata, links, commands and package README coverage\n  -> @taxkit/docs-fumadocs tests\n  -> apps/docs build and browser screenshots when rendering changes\n  -> bun run verification\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep public docs generic to callers and applications.\n- Do not document private downstream product strategy here.\n- Link to canonical architecture docs rather than duplicating them.\n- Treat old planning material as historical until revalidated.\n- Use [Documentation style](../standards/documentation-style.md) and the\n  related standards suite before writing or reviewing public docs.\n- Keep public MDX pages task-first. Use architecture docs for durable\n  ownership and runtime detail.\n- Validate public MDX through `@taxkit/docs-content`, which owns Effect Schema\n  frontmatter, navigation coverage, source-text policy, local link, MDX\n  component allowlist, examples and OpenAPI reference checks.\n- `draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate public\n  documentation; it is not accepted-current truth, publication, deployment,\n  external availability, correctness, or user visibility. `published` means\n  explicitly accepted current public documentation; it still does not establish\n  runtime or external availability. Preserve draft pages unless explicit\n  page-level acceptance records their transition.\n- Keep reusable Fumadocs code in `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs`; keep TaxKit\n  content contracts in `@taxkit/docs-content`; keep route composition and\n  app-specific rendering in `apps/docs`.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\n- [../product-specs/index.md](../product-specs/index.md)\n\n## Generated collection boundary\n\nGenerated collection adapters expose named Effect operations with safe tagged\nfailures. The collection owner wraps synchronous loader calls and processed-text\nPromise reads, preserving the SDK receiver. The reusable Fumadocs live Layer\ndecodes raw representations through its owning Schemas. Shiki metadata\ntransformation returns replacement nodes instead of mutating SDK-owned input.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":5042},"formatted_output":"\n```ts\nTests: docs structure\n\ndocs implementation\n  -> @taxkit/docs-content validate\n    -> frontmatter and navigation schema decode\n    -> navigation coverage and local link checks\n    -> MDX component allowlist\n    -> examples and OpenAPI reference checks\n  -> bun run check:docs\n  -> public/maintainer path separation and accepted status representation\n    -> generated Fumadocs and OpenAPI owner edges\n    -> maintainer metadata, links, commands and package README coverage\n  -> @taxkit/docs-fumadocs tests\n  -> apps/docs build and browser screenshots when rendering changes\n  -> bun run verification\n```\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- Keep public docs generic to callers and applications.\n- Do not document private downstream product strategy here.\n- Link to canonical architecture docs rather than duplicating them.\n- Treat old planning material as historical until revalidated.\n- Use [Documentation style](../standards/documentation-style.md) and the\n  related standards suite before writing or reviewing public docs.\n- Keep public MDX pages task-first. Use architecture docs for durable\n  ownership and runtime detail.\n- Validate public MDX through `@taxkit/docs-content`, which owns Effect Schema\n  frontmatter, navigation coverage, source-text policy, local link, MDX\n  component allowlist, examples and OpenAPI reference checks.\n- `draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate public\n  documentation; it is not accepted-current truth, publication, deployment,\n  external availability, correctness, or user visibility. `published` means\n  explicitly accepted current public documentation; it still does not establish\n  runtime or external availability. Preserve draft pages unless explicit\n  page-level acceptance records their transition.\n- Keep reusable Fumadocs code in `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs`; keep TaxKit\n  content contracts in `@taxkit/docs-content`; keep route composition and\n  app-specific rendering in `apps/docs`.\n\n## Related docs\n\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\n- [../product-specs/index.md](../product-specs/index.md)\n\n## Generated collection boundary\n\nGenerated collection adapters expose named Effect operations with safe tagged\nfailures. The collection owner wraps synchronous loader calls and processed-text\nPromise reads, preserving the SDK receiver. The reusable Fumadocs live Layer\ndecodes raw representations through its owning Schemas. Shiki metadata\ntransformation returns replacement nodes instead of mutating SDK-owned input.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311292965,"completed_at_ms":1791311292965}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:28:13.032Z","ordinal":50414,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a11279-2a68-7681-94bc-80de28c176b4","call_id":"call_f6624566cc3e4db4a29e31976a477891","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"fcab1d\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":248,\"output\":\"web test:native-pair: \\nweb test:native-pair: stdout | test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts > built native API and Website > uses the real API through the binding and browser, including an idle form and no JavaScript\\nweb test:native-pair: [05:27:54.132] ERROR (#2): Error [AssertionError]: expected 204 to be 200 // Object.is equality\\nweb test:native-pair:     at /Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit/apps/web/test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts:379:33 {\\nweb test:native-pair:   actual: 204,\\nweb test:native-pair:   expected: 200,\\nweb test:native-pair:   showDiff: true,\\nweb test:native-pair:   operator: 'strictEqual',\\nweb test:native-pair:   [cause]: undefined\\nweb test:native-pair: }\\nweb test:native-pair: \\nweb test:native-pair:  ❯ test/native-pair.boundary.test.ts (1 test | 1 failed) 3051ms\\nweb test:native-pair:    ❯ built native API and Website (1)\\nweb test:native-pair:      × uses the real API through the binding and browser, including an idle form and no JavaScript 3050ms\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"cd9ae0\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005375,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":961,\"output\":\"\\nCalculator-owned context, help and filter fields use `Option<Option<A>>` in\\nchecked TypeScript values: `None` means a missing key, `Some(None)` means a\\npresent undefined key, and `Some(Some(value))` means a present value. Owning\\nconstructors default omitted keys to `None`. JSON and HTTP query fields retain\\ntheir ordinary optional representation. Flatten the two absent forms only where\\nthey mean the same thing; do not invent a jurisdiction or tax year.\\n\\nSDK constructor-input aliases retain the selected descriptor facts relation.\\nThe SDK checks context/help through their owning Schemas and leaves facts to\\nthe selected calculator decoder. HTTP/RPC use canonical Types internally and\\nrepresentation codecs at serialisation. Their existing wire/OpenAPI fields and\\nvalues remain the compatibility contract.\\n\\n\\nCore calculation errors now retain diagnostic-key identity through nested\\nOptions. Current rule errors omit diagnostics; historical opaque/null values\\nremain codec values and are not safe telemetry. Catalogue entries use their\\nchecked selected continuation without the unused generic `program` field.\\nThe fresh package declarations change deliberately; retained HTTP/RPC, report,\\nmetadata and table/source values stay fixed. The active plan and domain-contract\\nreceipt own qualification; native rate admission below still needs whole-slice\\nqualification before T004 can close.\\n\\n\\n## Native calculation rate admission\\n\\nThe [calculator rate owner](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) defines canonical errors and a redacted IP key. The [native API](../../apps/api/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) composes admission once below bounded work, so HTTP/RPC/private Website calls share an allowance and each batch member takes one unit. Metadata remains independent. HTTP uses 429 with `Retry-After: 60` or fixed 503 guidance; RPC revision 4 preserves the same errors. The standalone Bun host and local engine/SDK keep their existing behaviour. Packed declarations must expose the expanded checked error union without adding private host identity capabilities to the published RPC exports.\\n\\n### Native documentation RPC\\n\\nThe same API POST endpoint mounts four documentation procedures through\\n`TaxKitPublicRpcGroup`, composed with the unchanged nine-procedure calculator\\ngroup. Documentation has its own `DocsRpcClient` and revision 1; calculator\\nrevision 4 and its required client methods are preserved. The server requires\\nboth owning services, supplied once at API composition. The content handlers\\nreuse the generated accepted catalogue and canonical values; they run no\\ncalculation and take no calculator allowance.\\n\\nBoth private client groups share the native scoped 2 MiB response reader, then\\nproject its private marker into their own errors. Documentation calls have a\\nten-second complete-response deadline, caller cancellation, credential/redirect\\nand tracing policy, checked version skew and decoder-only invalid-reply marker.\\nTheir fixed page/search errors and public-path bound belong to `@taxkit/content`\\nand are shared with HTTP. Native fatal defects retain the existing safe global\\nliteral; procedure defects use the declared documentation literal. Defects stay\\ndefects. The Website now supplies that client over its private binding and\\nuses browser-safe compiled MDX presentation. Its native GET loader transports\\nonly a bounded public page identity; original SSR pathnames own page selection.\\nThere is no authored-source fallback in the Website. Its `/search` form uses\\nthe same named `searchDocs` operation, term and result limits. Browser native\\nGET carries an ASCII URI component header; original SSR words cannot be\\noverridden by that header. Empty words skip the operation. The private app\\nconnection changes no public HTTP/RPC contract. Discovery remains T005 work.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"030ab9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005459,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":643,\"output\":\"\\nRevision `4` preserves canonical `CalculatorRateLimited` and `CalculatorAdmissionUnavailable` alongside existing expected errors. Older clients receive the checked revision mismatch. The native API and Website share the [calculator-owned rate contract](../../calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission); each batch calculation takes one unit and metadata takes none. `./rate-identity` is an explicit workspace-only host export; it is excluded from the published RPC capability surface. The rate identity is separate from RPC request JSON and is never an analytics identifier.\\n\\n## Documentation connection\\n\\n`./content/group`, `./content/schemas`, `./content/errors`, `./content/service`,\\n`./content/handlers`, `./content/live` and `./content/test` own four named calls:\\n`getNavigation`, `getPage`, `getMarkdown` and `searchPages`. Their native procedure\\ntags are `GetDocsNavigation`, `GetDocsPage`, `GetDocsMarkdown` and `SearchDocsPages`.\\nThe combined server group admits these alongside the existing nine calculator\\nprocedures. Calculator clients and revision 4 stay unchanged; documentation\\ncalls require their own revision 1 and fail with `DocsRpcVersionMismatch` during\\nversion skew. There is no automatic retry or backend fallback.\\n\\n`DocsRpcClientLive` takes the existing checked API origin and caller-supplied\\nHttpClient. Each call owns its native receive-loop scope, the ten-second whole\\nreply deadline and the same private 2 MiB byte reader as calculator calls. That\\nreader stops before an oversized tail, releases request/body resources and\\nkeeps the native parser and response Schemas. Both clients map its private size\\nmarker to their own fixed error. Request credentials, redirects and tracing\\nuse the same qualified policy. Independent adapter defects remain defects.\\n\\nHandlers capture the supplied `ContentService` once and return its immutable\\nvalues. Public missing-page and source-search errors use the content owner's\\nfixed errors. The documentation procedure defect is a fixed literal; the native\\nglobal fatal path retains its already qualified fixed literal. Internal source\\ndiagnostics and raw Causes are not response values. The native API supplies the\\nsame generated catalogue for HTTP and RPC. This package imports only compiled\\ncontent contracts, with no MDX compiler or source collection dependency.\\n\\nFocused documentation tests cover all four calls, valid and incompatible\\nversions, safe expected/global/procedure failures, damaged replies, unrelated\\nadapter defects, exact/oversized encoded byte limits, headers/body deadlines,\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":3,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"502e70\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000006208,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1459,\"output\":\"\\nThe private request omits an explicit AbortSignal because the pinned native RPC cannot serialise it. Client cancellation stops local waiting; API work and reply budgets remain in force. This does not prove remote cancellation. The guarded disposable root selects `local-emulator` and one loopback allowance; hosted composition defaults to `edge`. [Infrastructure configuration](../../packages/infrastructure/README.md#native-calculation-limiter-configuration) owns this distinction.\\n\\nThe native pair test also uses the separate checked documentation RPC client\\nagainst the actual built API. It compares navigation, every one of the 61\\naccepted pages and exact Markdown, plus bounded search across separate Worker\\nrequests. The same saved journey now qualifies the Website page connection described below.\\nSearch interaction is described below. Discovery and retirement of the old app remain T005 work.\\n\\n## Documentation pages\\n\\nThe catch-all route renders every accepted public page through the checked\\nprivate documentation client. Server rendering reads the original pathname;\\nrequest headers cannot select a different page. Browser navigation uses the\\nnative data-free GET function with one bounded `x-taxkit-docs-page` header.\\nIts generated URL is admitted beside the settings function. Both reject query\\npayloads, unsupported methods and content-type input before framework parsing;\\ninvalid public page addresses receive empty 400 responses.\\n\\nThe route's dedicated browser-safe boundary restores checked loader outcomes.\\nThe route matches that result before composing its sidebar and article. One\\napp-owned MDX map supplies internal router links, heading focus, code, images\\nand keyboard-focusable table scrolling. Initial hydration keeps the reader's\\nfocus. Ordinary navigation moves focus to the new page heading. Missing pages\\nuse the native not-found state and HTTP 404. Expected failures offer a fixed\\nmessage and an explicit recovery link.\\n\\nThe Vite build uses the existing content collection configuration and matching\\nMDX compiler. Browser code imports only compiled presentation and checked\\ncontracts. Before display, compiled Markdown and frontmatter must match the\\nAPI page exactly; a different body, metadata or missing module produces fixed\\nsafe guidance. Canonical URLs use the checked Website origin. The article's\\nMarkdown link opens the API's existing checked Markdown endpoint.\\n\\nThe native pair checks actual HTML for all 61 pages, native GET admission,\\nthree source-built content mismatches, malformed browser transport, real\\nsidebar/MDX navigation without document reload, heading focus, mobile\\nnavigation, table keyboard focus and reading without JavaScript. Saved local\\nimages supplement those checks. The [Website documentation receipt](../../docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json)\\nrecords their scope. Discovery files, share images and old-app retirement\\nare separate unfinished work. No local check establishes public availability.\\n\\nThe application router supplies the named documentation page loader through\\nits typed router context, beside the settings and search loaders. The page route consumes\\nthat function without importing its server-only implementation. Standalone\\nbrowser checks use the same route tree with supplied loaders; native built\\nchecks exercise the actual server function and private API connection.\\n\\n\\n## Documentation search\\n\\n`/search` has a labelled plain GET form with one `term` field. It works with\\nand without JavaScript and calls the same accepted-catalogue `searchDocs`\\noperation as the API. Empty words show an invitation to search; matching pages\\nshow their accepted titles and descriptions; no matches and unavailable search\\nhave separate guidance. Results link to the existing documentation routes.\\nSearch pages use `noindex, follow` and contain no calculation values.\\n\\nThe content owner keeps the 100-character term and twenty-result limits. The\\nWebsite checks its original URL once: duplicate or unexpected keys and excess\\nlength fail with fixed input guidance. Its router preserves literal URL pairs,\\nso words such as `1e3`, quoted text and Unicode cannot turn into JSON values.\\nThe native browser GET carries a bounded ASCII URI component in\\n`x-taxkit-docs-search`; the installed Schema codec encodes and decodes Unicode.\\nSSR uses the original URL, so a forged header cannot change the search words.\\nOnly the generated settings, page and search function addresses are admitted.\\nNative search query payloads, content types and malformed headers reject before\\nframework parsing; checked input failures never expose decoding diagnostics.\\n\\nThe search route restores its encoded outcome through its own checked boundary,\\nthen matches it before composing readonly form and result leaves. The typed\\nroute context supplies the named loader without importing server code into a\\nbrowser route. Search links share the existing heading-focus policy; a normal\\nHTML form submission remains an ordinary GET. No second index, personalised\\nresult store or collection event is added. The existing native journey checks\\nreal API results, literal words, hostile input, unavailable search, damaged\\ntransport, keyboard/phone behaviour and JavaScript-free form submission.\\nThe [search receipt](../../docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json)\\nrecords qualification separately from deployment and public availability.\\n\\nThe saved local-development check waits up to fifteen seconds for the Website\\nto serve a page after its address is printed. Only startup 502 or 503 responses\\nare retried; other errors fail immediately. The following actual browser\\nnavigation must still return 200 and show the expected page. This is a bounded\\nreadiness condition, not evidence of the cause of an earlier hosted 502.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":4,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3aebc1\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000005042,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":631,\"output\":\"\\n```ts\\nTests: docs structure\\n\\ndocs implementation\\n  -> @taxkit/docs-content validate\\n    -> frontmatter and navigation schema decode\\n    -> navigation coverage and local link checks\\n    -> MDX component allowlist\\n    -> examples and OpenAPI reference checks\\n  -> bun run check:docs\\n  -> public/maintainer path separation and accepted status representation\\n    -> generated Fumadocs and OpenAPI owner edges\\n    -> maintainer metadata, links, commands and package README coverage\\n  -> @taxkit/docs-fumadocs tests\\n  -> apps/docs build and browser screenshots when rendering changes\\n  -> bun run verification\\n```\\n\\n## Guardrails\\n\\n- Keep public docs generic to callers and applications.\\n- Do not document private downstream product strategy here.\\n- Link to canonical architecture docs rather than duplicating them.\\n- Treat old planning material as historical until revalidated.\\n- Use [Documentation style](../standards/documentation-style.md) and the\\n  related standards suite before writing or reviewing public docs.\\n- Keep public MDX pages task-first. Use architecture docs for durable\\n  ownership and runtime detail.\\n- Validate public MDX through `@taxkit/docs-content`, which owns Effect Schema\\n  frontmatter, navigation coverage, source-text policy, local link, MDX\\n  component allowlist, examples and OpenAPI reference checks.\\n- `draft` means authored, locally renderable, visibly labelled candidate public\\n  documentation; it is not accepted-current truth, publication, deployment,\\n  external availability, correctness, or user visibility. `published` means\\n  explicitly accepted current public documentation; it still does not establish\\n  runtime or external availability. Preserve draft pages unless explicit\\n  page-level acceptance records their transition.\\n- Keep reusable Fumadocs code in `@taxkit/docs-fumadocs`; keep TaxKit\\n  content contracts in `@taxkit/docs-content`; keep route composition and\\n  app-specific rendering in `apps/docs`.\\n\\n## Related docs\\n\\n- [API and SDK](./api-and-sdk.md)\\n- [Package ownership](./package-ownership.md)\\n- [../product-specs/index.md](../product-specs/index.md)\\n\\n## Generated collection boundary\\n\\nGenerated collection adapters expose named Effect operations with safe tagged\\nfailures. The collection owner wraps synchronous loader calls and processed-text\\nPromise reads, preserving the SDK receiver. The reusable Fumadocs live Layer\\ndecodes raw representations through its owning Schemas. Shiki metadata\\ntransformation returns replacement nodes instead of mutating SDK-owned input.\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791311293.032454}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
