 The root\n  restores encoded outcomes. Tax rules and calculations remain package/API-owned;\n  the three calculator pages and bounded T003 connection are locally qualified.\n  The same app owns checked documentation page loaders, app-specific MDX\n  composition, navigation/focus and responsive reading. Search, discovery and\n  retirement of `apps/docs` remain T005 work.\n\n`apps/docs`\n: Implemented public documentation app. It owns TanStack Start routes, the\n  docs app shell, route loaders, navigation presentation and app-local\n  MDX component composition, Schema-decoded build target, Cloudflare Vite\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311610025,"completed_at_ms":1791311610025}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:33:30.140Z","ordinal":50491,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b2a1a236-b0bc-4c48-82e3-9ad94ee40662","process_id":"85371","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '177,200p' docs/architecture/package-ownership.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '177,200p' docs/architecture/package-ownership.md","name":"package-ownership.md","path":"docs/architecture/package-ownership.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"instance owns one router and calculator service; incoming requests own body\nlimits, dispatch and cleanup. HTTP and RPC share the named calculator service operations.\nThe private `api/worker` export supplies native composition to the infrastructure\ngraph. The Website uses its private binding for SSR and checked public origin\nfor browser RPC; T003 is locally accepted by its dated connection acceptance review.\nT009 exported tracing and provider/deployment proof remain open.\n\n`packages/content`\n: Private compiled owner of canonical docs page/navigation contracts, source\n  errors, the accepted public catalogue Schema and `ContentService`. Application\n  composition injects one checked catalogue; the service reads accepted pages,\n  navigation and bounded search without filesystem or runtime execution. This\n  owner does not perform source acceptance or compile MDX. HTTP and native RPC\n  content groups consume this compiled contract instead of the source-only\n  Fumadocs collection. The public path refinement and fixed page/search errors\n  have one owner here.\n\n`packages/docs-content`\n: Implemented private source-only content package. It owns TaxKit docs\n  authored MDX, authored navigation, meta, validation issues,\n  validation errors, `DocsContentService`, the Fumadocs `source.config.ts`\n  and the generated `.source/*` boundary. Its schema/error exports retain\n  compatibility re-exports from `@taxkit/content`. Navigation decoding is independent\n  of the Node-only validation module. Validation and generated raw-text access\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"instance owns one router and calculator service; incoming requests own body\nlimits, dispatch and cleanup. HTTP and RPC share the named calculator service operations.\nThe private `api/worker` export supplies native composition to the infrastructure\ngraph. The Website uses its private binding for SSR and checked public origin\nfor browser RPC; T003 is locally accepted by its dated connection acceptance review.\nT009 exported tracing and provider/deployment proof remain open.\n\n`packages/content`\n: Private compiled owner of canonical docs page/navigation contracts, source\n  errors, the accepted public catalogue Schema and `ContentService`. Application\n  composition injects one checked catalogue; the service reads accepted pages,\n  navigation and bounded search without filesystem or runtime execution. This\n  owner does not perform source acceptance or compile MDX. HTTP and native RPC\n  content groups consume this compiled contract instead of the source-only\n  Fumadocs collection. The public path refinement and fixed page/search errors\n  have one owner here.\n\n`packages/docs-content`\n: Implemented private source-only content package. It owns TaxKit docs\n  authored MDX, authored navigation, meta, validation issues,\n  validation errors, `DocsContentService`, the Fumadocs `source.config.ts`\n  and the generated `.source/*` boundary. Its schema/error exports retain\n  compatibility re-exports from `@taxkit/content`. Navigation decoding is independent\n  of the Node-only validation module. Validation and generated raw-text access\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7083},"formatted_output":"instance owns one router and calculator service; incoming requests own body\nlimits, dispatch and cleanup. HTTP and RPC share the named calculator service operations.\nThe private `api/worker` export supplies native composition to the infrastructure\ngraph. The Website uses its private binding for SSR and checked public origin\nfor browser RPC; T003 is locally accepted by its dated connection acceptance review.\nT009 exported tracing and provider/deployment proof remain open.\n\n`packages/content`\n: Private compiled owner of canonical docs page/navigation contracts, source\n  errors, the accepted public catalogue Schema and `ContentService`. Application\n  composition injects one checked catalogue; the service reads accepted pages,\n  navigation and bounded search without filesystem or runtime execution. This\n  owner does not perform source acceptance or compile MDX. HTTP and native RPC\n  content groups consume this compiled contract instead of the source-only\n  Fumadocs collection. The public path refinement and fixed page/search errors\n  have one owner here.\n\n`packages/docs-content`\n: Implemented private source-only content package. It owns TaxKit docs\n  authored MDX, authored navigation, meta, validation issues,\n  validation errors, `DocsContentService`, the Fumadocs `source.config.ts`\n  and the generated `.source/*` boundary. Its schema/error exports retain\n  compatibility re-exports from `@taxkit/content`. Navigation decoding is independent\n  of the Node-only validation module. Validation and generated raw-text access\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311610140,"completed_at_ms":1791311610140}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:33:30.251Z","ordinal":50492,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-192c869a-8538-4d5a-b3fb-ee2c2b19d41f","process_id":"25875","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 35 docs/architecture/effect-services.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 35 docs/architecture/effect-services.md","name":"effect-services.md","path":"docs/architecture/effect-services.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"own cleanup on every exit. Metadata remains outside calculation capacity, while\nall nine calls share the five-second completion budget. Lazy invocation counts\nmetadata construction within it. The HTTP-owned streamed body policy provides\nSchema-owned JSON errors or fixed HTML guidance at the host boundary. No\nrunner or live Layer is built inside a calculation, and no transport gains a\ncompeting application contract. The owning package records timeout and CPU limits.\n\n\nThe [RPC owner](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md#complete-named-operation-contract)\nexposes all nine existing calculator operations. Its private concrete native\noperation transformation shares scope/deadline/safe transport policy across\nthose named methods; application work remains at the calculator service. No\noperation constructs a Layer or runner, and callers receive no raw client.\n\n\n## Native calculation rate admission\n\n`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\n\n\nNative rate decoding is admitted at the exact original-address, private-call,\nprovider-reply and host-root owners in `oxlint.config.ts`. Its exact wire and\nredacted-key fixtures have separate decoder/encoder admissions. Actual CLI\nfixtures accept those owned crossings, reject encoder execution at production\ningress, reject runners at every admitted file and reject decoding in the\nnearby calculator admission Layer. No wildcard or new unknown-parameter\nexception is added. The Website Layer accepts the generated native Fetcher\ncapability; its settings boundary checks the richer API binding once.\n\nThe native documentation RPC handler Layer captures the same supplied\n`ContentService` as public HTTP. It owns no runtime or catalogue fallback. A\nseparate `DocsRpcClient` provides four closed named operations over native RPC,\nwith its own revision/error vocabulary and per-call resource scope. Only the\nconcrete closed JSON byte reader is shared with the calculator client; no raw\nclient callback or provider object enters either service contract.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"own cleanup on every exit. Metadata remains outside calculation capacity, while\nall nine calls share the five-second completion budget. Lazy invocation counts\nmetadata construction within it. The HTTP-owned streamed body policy provides\nSchema-owned JSON errors or fixed HTML guidance at the host boundary. No\nrunner or live Layer is built inside a calculation, and no transport gains a\ncompeting application contract. The owning package records timeout and CPU limits.\n\n\nThe [RPC owner](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md#complete-named-operation-contract)\nexposes all nine existing calculator operations. Its private concrete native\noperation transformation shares scope/deadline/safe transport policy across\nthose named methods; application work remains at the calculator service. No\noperation constructs a Layer or runner, and callers receive no raw client.\n\n\n## Native calculation rate admission\n\n`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\n\n\nNative rate decoding is admitted at the exact original-address, private-call,\nprovider-reply and host-root owners in `oxlint.config.ts`. Its exact wire and\nredacted-key fixtures have separate decoder/encoder admissions. Actual CLI\nfixtures accept those owned crossings, reject encoder execution at production\ningress, reject runners at every admitted file and reject decoding in the\nnearby calculator admission Layer. No wildcard or new unknown-parameter\nexception is added. The Website Layer accepts the generated native Fetcher\ncapability; its settings boundary checks the richer API binding once.\n\nThe native documentation RPC handler Layer captures the same supplied\n`ContentService` as public HTTP. It owns no runtime or catalogue fallback. A\nseparate `DocsRpcClient` provides four closed named operations over native RPC,\nwith its own revision/error vocabulary and per-call resource scope. Only the\nconcrete closed JSON byte reader is shared with the calculator client; no raw\nclient callback or provider object enters either service contract.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":6250},"formatted_output":"own cleanup on every exit. Metadata remains outside calculation capacity, while\nall nine calls share the five-second completion budget. Lazy invocation counts\nmetadata construction within it. The HTTP-owned streamed body policy provides\nSchema-owned JSON errors or fixed HTML guidance at the host boundary. No\nrunner or live Layer is built inside a calculation, and no transport gains a\ncompeting application contract. The owning package records timeout and CPU limits.\n\n\nThe [RPC owner](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md#complete-named-operation-contract)\nexposes all nine existing calculator operations. Its private concrete native\noperation transformation shares scope/deadline/safe transport policy across\nthose named methods; application work remains at the calculator service. No\noperation constructs a Layer or runner, and callers receive no raw client.\n\n\n## Native calculation rate admission\n\n`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\n\n\nNative rate decoding is admitted at the exact original-address, private-call,\nprovider-reply and host-root owners in `oxlint.config.ts`. Its exact wire and\nredacted-key fixtures have separate decoder/encoder admissions. Actual CLI\nfixtures accept those owned crossings, reject encoder execution at production\ningress, reject runners at every admitted file and reject decoding in the\nnearby calculator admission Layer. No wildcard or new unknown-parameter\nexception is added. The Website Layer accepts the generated native Fetcher\ncapability; its settings boundary checks the richer API binding once.\n\nThe native documentation RPC handler Layer captures the same supplied\n`ContentService` as public HTTP. It owns no runtime or catalogue fallback. A\nseparate `DocsRpcClient` provides four closed named operations over native RPC,\nwith its own revision/error vocabulary and per-call resource scope. Only the\nconcrete closed JSON byte reader is shared with the calculator client; no raw\nclient callback or provider object enters either service contract.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311610251,"completed_at_ms":1791311610251}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:33:30.362Z","ordinal":50493,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-42f2c580-6442-476e-8ce5-0d41d333b003","process_id":"10205","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","tail -n 75 docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"tail -n 75 docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md","name":"testing-and-quality.md","path":"docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"observe deadline through headers/body, earlier interruption and scope cleanup;\noperation ingress observes credential/redirect policy.\n\nThe native workerd/Chromium pair separately compares all 61 accepted pages and\nexact Markdown through this client at the built API, retaining every existing\ncalculator journey and public HTTP check. API/client tests do not establish\nWebsite rendering on their own. The extended native Website journey below\nqualifies local page rendering. Search interaction has its own qualification\nbelow; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\nremain unproved by these local slices.\n\n### Native Website documentation qualification\n\nThe existing native Website journey now reads actual SSR HTML for every accepted\npage and independently checks headings, substantive article content, navigation,\ntitle, description, canonical and Markdown link. A checked loader value alone\ncannot satisfy that oracle. Requests carry a hostile page header to prove that\nSSR still uses the original address. Generated native page GET ingress accepts\nonly a checked public page header; malformed paths, query and content-type\ninput reject before framework parsing. Direct missing-page requests must return\nnative HTML 404.\n\nThree source-built API artifacts change an otherwise valid page's Markdown,\nfrontmatter or compiled-module identity. Each cold Website must return safe\nrecoverable HTML and a checked native loader failure. This exposed a cross-request\nstream in the installed Fetcher adapter; preserving the native JSON byte body\nrestored the intended failure path. A genuine valid server-function reply is\nalso damaged in Chromium to prove the route restoration boundary rejects it.\nThe native builder restores its actual source owners in a scope.\n\nReal sidebar and authored links must use native GET requests with zero document\nrequests, one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus. Initial\nhydration must not steal focus. Mobile navigation, table keyboard focus,\ncontained horizontal content and no-JavaScript reading are observed separately.\nFull-page desktop/mobile images start at the document top and supplement these\nfunctional checks. Browser bundle exclusion uses a positively observed API\nservice identity; a calculator service name appearing in accepted documentation\nprose is not executable engine code. Exact decoder consumers and neighbouring\nrenderer restrictions are exercised by the actual lint command.\n\n\n### Native Website search qualification\n\nThe existing native pair reads the built search function identity, checks its\nexact ingress and compares real SSR result titles with the actual API search\noperation. Literal numbers, quoted text and Unicode stay unchanged. Original\nSSR words resist forged headers; duplicate/unexpected keys, overlong words,\nmalformed URI components and invalid UTF-8 fail safely. Empty words, no matches\nand actual unavailable API settings have distinct rendered states. A genuine\nnative reply is damaged in Chromium to prove restoration rejects it.\n\nActual search navigation uses native GET without replacing the document;\nstandard GET form submission and document links also work without JavaScript.\nDesktop/phone captures supplement keyboard focus, contained content and result\nnavigation assertions. The focused browser fixture mounts the actual search\nloader/components in a scoped detached plain shell: rendered-value checks\nneed no insertion into the runner document. Actual page/focus/form observations\nremain in the native journey. It waits for the rendered form after navigation,\nthen checks restored words and duplicate-key rejection. A router promise alone\nis not an observation that React has finished showing its destination.\n\nExact lint selectors admit URL ingress decoding only in the search-location\nboundary, output encoding in the existing native loader host, and one restore\nconsumer in the search route. Actual CLI positive and neighbouring-renderer\nnegative cases retain the runtime/decoder/composition restrictions. The native\nsearch operation and content contract remain unchanged; no separate index or\nanalytics is qualified. The [dated search receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json)\nkeeps failures, fresh qualification and retained source identities separately.\n\nThe real local-development fixture requires served-page readiness after printed\naddresses. It retries only 502/503 responses at 100-millisecond intervals for at\nmost fifteen seconds, then requires 200 before strict browser navigation and\nheading observation. Application errors, socket errors and persistent gateway\nfailures still fail. This strengthens the start condition without diagnosing\nan earlier hosted 502 or establishing that its cause has been reproduced.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"observe deadline through headers/body, earlier interruption and scope cleanup;\noperation ingress observes credential/redirect policy.\n\nThe native workerd/Chromium pair separately compares all 61 accepted pages and\nexact Markdown through this client at the built API, retaining every existing\ncalculator journey and public HTTP check. API/client tests do not establish\nWebsite rendering on their own. The extended native Website journey below\nqualifies local page rendering. Search interaction has its own qualification\nbelow; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\nremain unproved by these local slices.\n\n### Native Website documentation qualification\n\nThe existing native Website journey now reads actual SSR HTML for every accepted\npage and independently checks headings, substantive article content, navigation,\ntitle, description, canonical and Markdown link. A checked loader value alone\ncannot satisfy that oracle. Requests carry a hostile page header to prove that\nSSR still uses the original address. Generated native page GET ingress accepts\nonly a checked public page header; malformed paths, query and content-type\ninput reject before framework parsing. Direct missing-page requests must return\nnative HTML 404.\n\nThree source-built API artifacts change an otherwise valid page's Markdown,\nfrontmatter or compiled-module identity. Each cold Website must return safe\nrecoverable HTML and a checked native loader failure. This exposed a cross-request\nstream in the installed Fetcher adapter; preserving the native JSON byte body\nrestored the intended failure path. A genuine valid server-function reply is\nalso damaged in Chromium to prove the route restoration boundary rejects it.\nThe native builder restores its actual source owners in a scope.\n\nReal sidebar and authored links must use native GET requests with zero document\nrequests, one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus. Initial\nhydration must not steal focus. Mobile navigation, table keyboard focus,\ncontained horizontal content and no-JavaScript reading are observed separately.\nFull-page desktop/mobile images start at the document top and supplement these\nfunctional checks. Browser bundle exclusion uses a positively observed API\nservice identity; a calculator service name appearing in accepted documentation\nprose is not executable engine code. Exact decoder consumers and neighbouring\nrenderer restrictions are exercised by the actual lint command.\n\n\n### Native Website search qualification\n\nThe existing native pair reads the built search function identity, checks its\nexact ingress and compares real SSR result titles with the actual API search\noperation. Literal numbers, quoted text and Unicode stay unchanged. Original\nSSR words resist forged headers; duplicate/unexpected keys, overlong words,\nmalformed URI components and invalid UTF-8 fail safely. Empty words, no matches\nand actual unavailable API settings have distinct rendered states. A genuine\nnative reply is damaged in Chromium to prove restoration rejects it.\n\nActual search navigation uses native GET without replacing the document;\nstandard GET form submission and document links also work without JavaScript.\nDesktop/phone captures supplement keyboard focus, contained content and result\nnavigation assertions. The focused browser fixture mounts the actual search\nloader/components in a scoped detached plain shell: rendered-value checks\nneed no insertion into the runner document. Actual page/focus/form observations\nremain in the native journey. It waits for the rendered form after navigation,\nthen checks restored words and duplicate-key rejection. A router promise alone\nis not an observation that React has finished showing its destination.\n\nExact lint selectors admit URL ingress decoding only in the search-location\nboundary, output encoding in the existing native loader host, and one restore\nconsumer in the search route. Actual CLI positive and neighbouring-renderer\nnegative cases retain the runtime/decoder/composition restrictions. The native\nsearch operation and content contract remain unchanged; no separate index or\nanalytics is qualified. The [dated search receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json)\nkeeps failures, fresh qualification and retained source identities separately.\n\nThe real local-development fixture requires served-page readiness after printed\naddresses. It retries only 502/503 responses at 100-millisecond intervals for at\nmost fifteen seconds, then requires 200 before strict browser navigation and\nheading observation. Application errors, socket errors and persistent gateway\nfailures still fail. This strengthens the start condition without diagnosing\nan earlier hosted 502 or establishing that its cause has been reproduced.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7167},"formatted_output":"observe deadline through headers/body, earlier interruption and scope cleanup;\noperation ingress observes credential/redirect policy.\n\nThe native workerd/Chromium pair separately compares all 61 accepted pages and\nexact Markdown through this client at the built API, retaining every existing\ncalculator journey and public HTTP check. API/client tests do not establish\nWebsite rendering on their own. The extended native Website journey below\nqualifies local page rendering. Search interaction has its own qualification\nbelow; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\nremain unproved by these local slices.\n\n### Native Website documentation qualification\n\nThe existing native Website journey now reads actual SSR HTML for every accepted\npage and independently checks headings, substantive article content, navigation,\ntitle, description, canonical and Markdown link. A checked loader value alone\ncannot satisfy that oracle. Requests carry a hostile page header to prove that\nSSR still uses the original address. Generated native page GET ingress accepts\nonly a checked public page header; malformed paths, query and content-type\ninput reject before framework parsing. Direct missing-page requests must return\nnative HTML 404.\n\nThree source-built API artifacts change an otherwise valid page's Markdown,\nfrontmatter or compiled-module identity. Each cold Website must return safe\nrecoverable HTML and a checked native loader failure. This exposed a cross-request\nstream in the installed Fetcher adapter; preserving the native JSON byte body\nrestored the intended failure path. A genuine valid server-function reply is\nalso damaged in Chromium to prove the route restoration boundary rejects it.\nThe native builder restores its actual source owners in a scope.\n\nReal sidebar and authored links must use native GET requests with zero document\nrequests, one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus. Initial\nhydration must not steal focus. Mobile navigation, table keyboard focus,\ncontained horizontal content and no-JavaScript reading are observed separately.\nFull-page desktop/mobile images start at the document top and supplement these\nfunctional checks. Browser bundle exclusion uses a positively observed API\nservice identity; a calculator service name appearing in accepted documentation\nprose is not executable engine code. Exact decoder consumers and neighbouring\nrenderer restrictions are exercised by the actual lint command.\n\n\n### Native Website search qualification\n\nThe existing native pair reads the built search function identity, checks its\nexact ingress and compares real SSR result titles with the actual API search\noperation. Literal numbers, quoted text and Unicode stay unchanged. Original\nSSR words resist forged headers; duplicate/unexpected keys, overlong words,\nmalformed URI components and invalid UTF-8 fail safely. Empty words, no matches\nand actual unavailable API settings have distinct rendered states. A genuine\nnative reply is damaged in Chromium to prove restoration rejects it.\n\nActual search navigation uses native GET without replacing the document;\nstandard GET form submission and document links also work without JavaScript.\nDesktop/phone captures supplement keyboard focus, contained content and result\nnavigation assertions. The focused browser fixture mounts the actual search\nloader/components in a scoped detached plain shell: rendered-value checks\nneed no insertion into the runner document. Actual page/focus/form observations\nremain in the native journey. It waits for the rendered form after navigation,\nthen checks restored words and duplicate-key rejection. A router promise alone\nis not an observation that React has finished showing its destination.\n\nExact lint selectors admit URL ingress decoding only in the search-location\nboundary, output encoding in the existing native loader host, and one restore\nconsumer in the search route. Actual CLI positive and neighbouring-renderer\nnegative cases retain the runtime/decoder/composition restrictions. The native\nsearch operation and content contract remain unchanged; no separate index or\nanalytics is qualified. The [dated search receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json)\nkeeps failures, fresh qualification and retained source identities separately.\n\nThe real local-development fixture requires served-page readiness after printed\naddresses. It retries only 502/503 responses at 100-millisecond intervals for at\nmost fifteen seconds, then requires 200 before strict browser navigation and\nheading observation. Application errors, socket errors and persistent gateway\nfailures still fail. This strengthens the start condition without diagnosing\nan earlier hosted 502 or establishing that its cause has been reproduced.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311610362,"completed_at_ms":1791311610362}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:33:30.473Z","ordinal":50494,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3b420172-4754-4295-80b2-e3a01e288fd6","process_id":"59849","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'taxkit-native-website|2026-10-07-website-docs-search' docs/verification/critical-journeys.json"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'taxkit-native-website|2026-10-07-website-docs-search' docs/verification/critical-journeys.json","query":"taxkit-native-website|2026-10-07-website-docs-search","path":"critical-journeys.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"155:      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n215:        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\"\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"155:      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n215:        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\"\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":8542},"formatted_output":"155:      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n215:        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\"\n"},"started_at_ms":1791311610473,"completed_at_ms":1791311610473}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:33:30.543Z","ordinal":50495,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1127e-02af-7c63-872f-672c0be4c826","call_id":"call_TbJ5B5tVNZFo7mzHfXKo6GCa","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0a3c88\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000875,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":428,\"output\":\"\\n## Scope\\n\\n`apps/api` owns process config, Bun server startup, request dispatch to\\n`@taxkit/api-http/server` and graceful shutdown. API contracts, handlers,\\nschemas, generated OpenAPI and docs routes stay in `packages/api/http`.\\n\\nBoth API hosts provide `ContentService` from the accepted generated catalogue.\\n`src/content.boundary.ts` imports only `@taxkit/docs-content/public-catalogue`\\nJSON, checks it once when the host is built and reports a fixed configuration\\nfailure if it is invalid. Incoming requests do not load authored MDX or run\\nthe compiler. Public HTTP and four native RPC documentation operations serve\\nnavigation, checked page values, bounded search and exact processed Markdown\\nfrom that same service. Documentation calls consume no calculator allowance.\\nSee the [HTTP package](../../packages/api/http/README.md) for paths/response rules\\nand the [RPC owner](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md#documentation-connection)\\nfor the separate documentation revision and client.\\n\\nThe API dependency build generates the accepted catalogue before TypeScript\\nor native bundling consumes it. Its ESNext module profile preserves the JSON\\nimport attribute for ordinary Node loading of emitted modules. The Website,\\ninfrastructure and Alchemy source-checking profiles also admit that attribute\\nwhen they inspect the API Worker source. Compiled public packages retain their\\nexisting module profiles.\\n\\nThe retained standalone smoke check reads page JSON, navigation, search and\\nMarkdown through the real HTTP process. It checks their common page address,\\ntitle and processed body within one five-second operation deadline, in addition\\nto the existing calculator and OpenAPI checks.\\n\\n## Native Worker candidate\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"fb1023\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":518,\"output\":\"\\n`packages/docs-fumadocs`\\n: Private reusable package for generic Fumadocs configuration, Effect Schema to\\n  Standard Schema bridging, the generic source service and live/test Layers,\\n  and generic MDX render primitives.\\n\\n`tools/documentation/owner-policy.json`\\n: Machine-readable separation between public content, maintainer documents,\\ngenerated artifacts, and authored SDK documentation. It validates accepted\\npublic-status representation and navigation ownership without claiming runtime\\nor external availability.\\n\\n`tools/documentation/catalogue.runtime.ts`\\n: Local accepted-catalogue build command (`bun run docs:catalogue`). It checks\\nversion-two records and exact source hashes before and after MDX processing,\\nomits drafts, checks navigation through the canonical catalogue constructor,\\nand writes ignored `.source/public-catalogue.json` only on success. No accepted\\npages is a failure. Source acceptance is recorded independently for each page\\nand navigation in the owner policy's exact bindings. Reviewed byte hashes\\nprevent a later edit from silently inheriting acceptance. The docs-content\\npackage build includes this step, with source-review records and the compiler's\\nbrowser path in its cache inputs. Its JSON-only `./public-catalogue` export is\\nchecked once by each API host; it imports no compiler into request handling.\\nHTTP and native RPC documentation groups delegate page/navigation/search and\\nprocessed Markdown to the same `ContentService`. Its compiled public-path\\nrefinement and fixed missing-page/search errors serve both transports. The\\nreplacement Website renders accepted pages using that private connection and\\nbrowser-safe compiled presentation. Its `/search` GET form uses the same named\\naccepted-catalogue search operation, showing accepted titles and descriptions\\nwith the existing document links. No second index is added. Discovery and\\nold-app retirement remain T005 work.\\n\\n`docs/architecture`\\n: Durable implementation architecture.\\n\\n`docs/product-specs`\\n: Current product/spec intent for repo development.\\n\\n## Public docs graph\\n\\n```ts\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"cdd98b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008292,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":313,\"output\":\"by their packages. It must not depend on `@taxkit/api-http`; HTTP\\ntransports call the calculator service directly; the SDK is a test-only\\ncomparison dependency of the HTTP package. Its Effect entrypoint owns\\nrequest-preserving calculator helpers such as `calculateRunRequest`,\\n`calculateReportRequest` and `calculateReport`, while reusing\\ncalculator-owned `CalculatorRun*` schemas and `CalculatorServiceError`.\\n\\n`apps/web`\\n: Native TanStack Website candidate. It owns form presentation/commands, the\\n  server runner and React Atom registry. The private server binding and checked\\n  public browser address reach the separate API through native RPC. The root\\n  restores encoded outcomes. Tax rules and calculations remain package/API-owned;\\n  the three calculator pages and bounded T003 connection are locally qualified.\\n  The same app owns checked documentation page loaders, app-specific MDX\\n  composition, navigation/focus and responsive reading. Search, discovery and\\n  retirement of `apps/docs` remain T005 work.\\n\\n`apps/docs`\\n: Implemented public documentation app. It owns TanStack Start routes, the\\n  docs app shell, route loaders, navigation presentation and app-local\\n  MDX component composition, Schema-decoded build target, Cloudflare Vite\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"36bcc3\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007083,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":385,\"output\":\"instance owns one router and calculator service; incoming requests own body\\nlimits, dispatch and cleanup. HTTP and RPC share the named calculator service operations.\\nThe private `api/worker` export supplies native composition to the infrastructure\\ngraph. The Website uses its private binding for SSR and checked public origin\\nfor browser RPC; T003 is locally accepted by its dated connection acceptance review.\\nT009 exported tracing and provider/deployment proof remain open.\\n\\n`packages/content`\\n: Private compiled owner of canonical docs page/navigation contracts, source\\n  errors, the accepted public catalogue Schema and `ContentService`. Application\\n  composition injects one checked catalogue; the service reads accepted pages,\\n  navigation and bounded search without filesystem or runtime execution. This\\n  owner does not perform source acceptance or compile MDX. HTTP and native RPC\\n  content groups consume this compiled contract instead of the source-only\\n  Fumadocs collection. The public path refinement and fixed page/search errors\\n  have one owner here.\\n\\n`packages/docs-content`\\n: Implemented private source-only content package. It owns TaxKit docs\\n  authored MDX, authored navigation, meta, validation issues,\\n  validation errors, `DocsContentService`, the Fumadocs `source.config.ts`\\n  and the generated `.source/*` boundary. Its schema/error exports retain\\n  compatibility re-exports from `@taxkit/content`. Navigation decoding is independent\\n  of the Node-only validation module. Validation and generated raw-text access\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0bad68\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":636,\"output\":\"own cleanup on every exit. Metadata remains outside calculation capacity, while\\nall nine calls share the five-second completion budget. Lazy invocation counts\\nmetadata construction within it. The HTTP-owned streamed body policy provides\\nSchema-owned JSON errors or fixed HTML guidance at the host boundary. No\\nrunner or live Layer is built inside a calculation, and no transport gains a\\ncompeting application contract. The owning package records timeout and CPU limits.\\n\\n\\nThe [RPC owner](../../packages/api/rpc/README.md#complete-named-operation-contract)\\nexposes all nine existing calculator operations. Its private concrete native\\noperation transformation shares scope/deadline/safe transport policy across\\nthose named methods; application work remains at the calculator service. No\\noperation constructs a Layer or runner, and callers receive no raw client.\\n\\n\\n## Native calculation rate admission\\n\\n`CalculatorAdmission` is a closed named service; its [owning contract](../../packages/calculators/README.md#native-calculation-rate-admission) and redacted key Schema live with calculators. The request Context reference carries checked identity separately from facts. `PublicCalculatorServiceRateLimited` provides calculation-only admission; the native API composes it once below bounded work. Its provider Layer, installed live Layer and mock test Layer remain separate. Native provider replies are decoded immediately and failures become fixed errors without provider causes or addresses.\\n\\n\\nNative rate decoding is admitted at the exact original-address, private-call,\\nprovider-reply and host-root owners in `oxlint.config.ts`. Its exact wire and\\nredacted-key fixtures have separate decoder/encoder admissions. Actual CLI\\nfixtures accept those owned crossings, reject encoder execution at production\\ningress, reject runners at every admitted file and reject decoding in the\\nnearby calculator admission Layer. No wildcard or new unknown-parameter\\nexception is added. The Website Layer accepts the generated native Fetcher\\ncapability; its settings boundary checks the richer API binding once.\\n\\nThe native documentation RPC handler Layer captures the same supplied\\n`ContentService` as public HTTP. It owns no runtime or catalogue fallback. A\\nseparate `DocsRpcClient` provides four closed named operations over native RPC,\\nwith its own revision/error vocabulary and per-call resource scope. Only the\\nconcrete closed JSON byte reader is shared with the calculator client; no raw\\nclient callback or provider object enters either service contract.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"61f4ef\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007167,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1202,\"output\":\"observe deadline through headers/body, earlier interruption and scope cleanup;\\noperation ingress observes credential/redirect policy.\\n\\nThe native workerd/Chromium pair separately compares all 61 accepted pages and\\nexact Markdown through this client at the built API, retaining every existing\\ncalculator journey and public HTTP check. API/client tests do not establish\\nWebsite rendering on their own. The extended native Website journey below\\nqualifies local page rendering. Search interaction has its own qualification\\nbelow; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\\nremain unproved by these local slices.\\n\\n### Native Website documentation qualification\\n\\nThe existing native Website journey now reads actual SSR HTML for every accepted\\npage and independently checks headings, substantive article content, navigation,\\ntitle, description, canonical and Markdown link. A checked loader value alone\\ncannot satisfy that oracle. Requests carry a hostile page header to prove that\\nSSR still uses the original address. Generated native page GET ingress accepts\\nonly a checked public page header; malformed paths, query and content-type\\ninput reject before framework parsing. Direct missing-page requests must return\\nnative HTML 404.\\n\\nThree source-built API artifacts change an otherwise valid page's Markdown,\\nfrontmatter or compiled-module identity. Each cold Website must return safe\\nrecoverable HTML and a checked native loader failure. This exposed a cross-request\\nstream in the installed Fetcher adapter; preserving the native JSON byte body\\nrestored the intended failure path. A genuine valid server-function reply is\\nalso damaged in Chromium to prove the route restoration boundary rejects it.\\nThe native builder restores its actual source owners in a scope.\\n\\nReal sidebar and authored links must use native GET requests with zero document\\nrequests, one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus. Initial\\nhydration must not steal focus. Mobile navigation, table keyboard focus,\\ncontained horizontal content and no-JavaScript reading are observed separately.\\nFull-page desktop/mobile images start at the document top and supplement these\\nfunctional checks. Browser bundle exclusion uses a positively observed API\\nservice identity; a calculator service name appearing in accepted documentation\\nprose is not executable engine code. Exact decoder consumers and neighbouring\\nrenderer restrictions are exercised by the actual lint command.\\n\\n\\n### Native Website search qualification\\n\\nThe existing native pair reads the built search function identity, checks its\\nexact ingress and compares real SSR result titles with the actual API search\\noperation. Literal numbers, quoted text and Unicode stay unchanged. Original\\nSSR words resist forged headers; duplicate/unexpected keys, overlong words,\\nmalformed URI components and invalid UTF-8 fail safely. Empty words, no matches\\nand actual unavailable API settings have distinct rendered states. A genuine\\nnative reply is damaged in Chromium to prove restoration rejects it.\\n\\nActual search navigation uses native GET without replacing the document;\\nstandard GET form submission and document links also work without JavaScript.\\nDesktop/phone captures supplement keyboard focus, contained content and result\\nnavigation assertions. The focused browser fixture mounts the actual search\\nloader/components in a scoped detached plain shell: rendered-value checks\\nneed no insertion into the runner document. Actual page/focus/form observations\\nremain in the native journey. It waits for the rendered form after navigation,\\nthen checks restored words and duplicate-key rejection. A router promise alone\\nis not an observation that React has finished showing its destination.\\n\\nExact lint selectors admit URL ingress decoding only in the search-location\\nboundary, output encoding in the existing native loader host, and one restore\\nconsumer in the search route. Actual CLI positive and neighbouring-renderer\\nnegative cases retain the runtime/decoder/composition restrictions. The native\\nsearch operation and content contract remain unchanged; no separate index or\\nanalytics is qualified. The [dated search receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json)\\nkeeps failures, fresh qualification and retained source identities separately.\\n\\nThe real local-development fixture requires served-page readiness after printed\\naddresses. It retries only 502/503 responses at 100-millisecond intervals for at\\nmost fifteen seconds, then requires 200 before strict browser navigation and\\nheading observation. Application errors, socket errors and persistent gateway\\nfailures still fail. This strengthens the start condition without diagnosing\\nan earlier hosted 502 or establishing that its cause has been reproduced.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"84943b\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000008542,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":35,\"output\":\"155:      \\\"id\\\": \\\"taxkit-native-website\\\",\\n215:        \\\"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\\\"\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791311610.543648}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
