ted sources.\n### T005 discovery implementation intent — 7 October\n\nSearch commit `8b32afca` passed complete local tests and verification and was\npushed to draft #155. Its own hosted Quality run `37509022712` remains pending\nat this observation. Metrics remain deferred.\n\nThe next slice derives `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt` and\n`/llms-full.txt` from the accepted catalogue in the backend content owner.\nNative Website addresses are deferred `Worker.URL` values, so the ordinary\nsource build cannot safely bake the actual stage origin into static files.\nOne closed discovery operation will use the application's already checked,\ncached Website settings at request time; the Website will return its checked\ndocument without owning a second catalogue or reading authored MDX. Public\norigin validation will have one shared Schema with separate API and Website\nidentities. No calculation values, invented modification dates, additional\ncache or collection event belong in these files.\n\nThe current llms.txt proposal, sitemap protocol and Google's crawler guidance\nwere read on 7 October. Agent links must lead to usable processed Markdown;\nthe current explicit API Markdown links can do this while same-page Markdown\nnegotiation remains a later slice. Robots controls crawling rather than access;\nsearch retains its noindex response/page policy. The actual configured origin,\ncomplete accepted-page coverage, text/media types, safe errors, request lifetime\nand old useful routes need local built-app proof before accepting this slice.\n\nDocumentation impact: Change required for content/API/RPC/Website contracts,\ntheir package guides, owning architecture, exact checks and current task/journey\npointers. Preserve source-bound acceptance, retained tax results, previous proof,\ndisabled collection and the older app until retirement proof. No new operational\ncommand or provider action is intended, so runbook applicability is N/A.\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"documentType\": \"bounded-proof-receipt\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"evidence\",\n  \"authority\": \"supporting\",\n  \"owner\": \"taxkit-web-app-owner\",\n  \"observedAt\": \"2026-10-06T18:07:15.169711+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"Local Website accepted-catalogue search qualified; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n  \"baseHead\": \"b7cbed17a0b52283b5f9f75abf68c448d73af390\",\n  \"actorAuthority\": {\n    \"principal\": \"Cooper\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex\",\n    \"operation\": \"Approved CSF-T005 implementation, local checks, tested commit/push and continuation of draft PR155\",\n    \"environment\": \"Local native workerd/Chromium pair and repository checks\",\n    \"approvalBoundary\": \"No merge, deploy, publication, provider apply or metrics implementation\"\n  },\n  \"outcome\": [\n    \"A labelled /search GET form uses the existing accepted-catalogue searchDocs operation, works without JavaScript and links checked title/description results to documentation.\",\n    \"Literal URL pairs preserve scientific numbers, quoted words, duplicate keys and Unicode; checked ingress rejects unexpected/duplicate keys and overlong words.\",\n    \"Generated native search GET takes no data or client Context, carries only a bounded ASCII URI header and decodes Unicode through the installed Schema codec. Original SSR URLs resist forged headers.\",\n    \"Empty words skip search. Empty/no-match/loading/invalid/unavailable states remain separate; damaged genuine browser replies fail checked restoration safely.\",\n    \"The route restores and matches encoded results before readonly leaf composition. Typed route context avoids server imports in a browser route. Existing heading-focus and phone navigation remain owned.\",\n    \"Local startup observes served-page readiness after printed addresses, retrying only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds before strict successful browser navigation. The earlier hosted 502 cause remains unknown.\"\n  ],\n  \"impact\": {\n    \"changeRequired\": [\n      \"apps/web source/Schema/URL/restoration/native-loader/host ingress and existing native/browser tests\",\n      \"Exact oxlint selectors and actual CLI positive/negative cases\",\n      \"apps/web/README.md; frontend, content-and-posts, API-and-SDK, Effect-services and testing-quality architecture\",\n      \"Active SPEC/tasks/plan, existing taxkit-native-website journey and this receipt\"\n    ],\n    \"preserve\": [\n      \"127 hashed sources: 61 accepted pages, 64 review records, navigation and four integration templates; 62 exact bindings and owner policy\",\n      \"Content service and HTTP/RPC contracts; retained calculator answers and Medicare scope decision\",\n      \"Existing visual design and historical docs/runtime receipts\",\n      \"Disabled platform collection and explicit metrics deferral\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": [\n      \"No package export/wire change or new Changeset; existing documentation contract Changeset retained\",\n      \"No new runbook command, operational procedure, skill installation or provider/credential/release change\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"bun\": \"1.4.2\",\n    \"node\": \"v24.16.0\",\n    \"effect\": \"4.0.0\",\n    \"alchemy\": \"2.0.0-beta.80\",\n    \"reactRouter\": \"1.170.41\",\n    \"routerCore\": \"1.171.34\",\n    \"vite\": \"8.3.2\",\n    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\",\n    \"host\": \"Local macOS arm64; selected Node/Bun and installed Chromium\",\n    \"referenceBoundary\": \"Earlier Effect and Alchemy upstream references retained; installed Effect URI codec, Alchemy Vite lifecycle and TanStack query/Transitioner source own compatibility. No dependency upgrade.\"\n  },\n  \"sourceIdentities\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/README.md\",\n      \"sha256\": \"5649d424841cfff2f4cea967b83c2b7cd3bc2ceadb94272ae2d524ba8ec22d95\",\n      \"bytes\": 23774\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/components.tsx\",\n      \"sha256\": \"85286f6e573ab5e85ab50e7a257445116e8609212f2bc5f0b43b34c1472297ac\",\n      \"bytes\": 3292\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/errors.ts\",\n      \"sha256\": \"b988591084342ae659c974856662d6bc852e5c247a4265d5f203eef5654fde10\",\n      \"bytes\": 755\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/page.view.tsx\",\n      \"sha256\": \"22178bf566c39bb3a5e022e2bf2bb57c5fee5c7ea51fa650c2a2f3d385d84efd\",\n      \"bytes\": 2276\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/route-boundary.ts\",\n      \"sha256\": \"211ff2bf309c6afb1df89003ea7e8a0b7b74c303ff7354009e285cf79ceb3331\",\n      \"bytes\": 884\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/search-location.boundary.ts\",\n      \"sha256\": \"f3ef7639c6e7cff836a062827d04bb32f7a12af9a596a56a2b1daf822db82875\",\n      \"bytes\": 1599\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"apps/web/src/lib/docs/search.view.tsx\",\n      \"sha256\": \"a9f2cd37c205b2762aaab77c643bb86c52c477abab429e51acad9f238b83600d\",\n      \"bytes\": 2020\n    },\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7791},"formatted_output":"docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md\ndocs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json\n      \"nonClaims\": [\n        \"Local closure is not approval for a tag, release, npm publication, deployment, provider access, or public availability.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"taxkit-native-website\",\n      \"actorOrConsumer\": \"Calculator Website visitor and documentation reader\",\n      \"boundary\": \"Built and live native Website/private API binding/direct browser RPC\",\n      \"startingState\": \"Selected Node and Chromium are available; local ports 4196\\u20134205 used by the native fixtures are available.\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        \"Native Alchemy source-built API and Website\",\n        \"Retained take-home example: 1654 dollars weekly, threshold claimed\",\n        \"Retained withholding example: 9500 dollars monthly, threshold not claimed\",\n        \"Retained annual example: 67000 dollars taxable income\",\n        \"Accepted 61-page documentation catalogue and matching compiled MDX presentation\"\n      ],\n      \"stepsOrProcedureOwner\": \"bun run web:test:native-pair\",\n      \"expectedBehavior\": [\n        \"Initial rendering makes no calculation; explicit Calculate produces 1301 dollars take-home pay through the private binding and direct browser POST /rpc.\",\n        \"Idle settings remain available; repeated Worker calls finish; editing cancels unfinished work and keeps the previous successful answer visibly out of date until a successful explicit calculation; the form also works without JavaScript.\",\n        \"Checked errors restore safely in the browser; native request limits and production import boundaries hold.\",\n        \"Data-free native settings GET succeeds; unexpected query/method input is rejected before framework parsing; an actual internal settings defect returns empty 500 and fixed safe logs.\",\n        \"Unknown, extended or missing native settings function addresses return empty 404 before framework lookup/logging; native generated URL owns identity.\",\n        \"Controlled slow headers and an unfinished actual reply reach the ten-second deadline; browser requests abort after the deadline, editing and browser Back leaving the form.\",\n        \"Real native CLI local development supplies both addresses/bindings, reloads API and Website source, restores exact sources and closes app ports on scoped shutdown.\",\n        \"Both actual saved local resources have explicitly disabled platform log/trace collection and zero sampling; source restoration uses the non-polling watcher and requires both visible page updates.\",\n        \"Take-home explanation opens with the keyboard without calculation; breakdown, recorded threshold and rule sources remain attached to the old report after form edits.\",\n        \"Catalogue-backed navigation offers all three calculators; withholding and annual pages start with their own empty result and return the retained 2756 and 12228 dollar answers through real browser RPC and standard HTML POST without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The new pages retain their own report and explanation after edits without another request; the annual Medicare limitation stays visible and the agent route links to actual API descriptions.\",\n        \"All supported native HTML form POST paths and public HTTP/RPC reject more than 64 KiB of encoded text with fixed safe HTML 413 form guidance or checked JSON 413 API guidance; public rejection preserves the Website CORS policy.\",\n        \"All nine closed named calculator RPC calls return checked canonical results; the seven additional metadata calls run through the real built API Worker.\",\n        \"Reached metadata work times out at five seconds through both actual HTTP and the generated RPC client; HTTP 504 keeps CORS and safe cleanup is observed. Metadata takes no calculation place.\",\n        \"All 61 accepted pages return real SSR articles with matching headings, navigation, title, description, canonical and checked Markdown link; missing public pages return native HTML 404.\",\n        \"Native data-free documentation GET accepts only bounded public page headers; original SSR addresses cannot be overridden by headers. Invalid query/content-type/page inputs reject before framework parsing.\",\n        \"Cold body/metadata/module mismatch and damaged native browser transport show safe recoverable guidance. Internal sidebar/authored links use native GET without document reload, with one current-page marker and deliberate heading focus; hydration preserves initial focus.\",\n        \"Mobile navigation and table scrolling work with the keyboard, horizontal content stays inside the article and ordinary documentation links work without JavaScript.\",\n        \"The accepted-catalogue search form retains literal URL words and Unicode, checks duplicate/unknown keys and bounded native URI headers, distinguishes empty/no-match/unavailable states and uses safe recoverable damaged-transport guidance.\",\n        \"Search native navigation retains the document; actual standard GET submission and result links work without JavaScript, with keyboard focus and contained phone layout.\",\n        \"After printed local addresses, served-page readiness retries only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds; actual browser navigation still requires 200 and its expected heading.\"\n      ],\n      \"expectedSideEffects\": [\n        \"Ignored native build files, scoped local Workers and Chromium only.\"\n      ],\n      \"preservedInvariants\": [\n        \"Retained tax results and existing docs operations stay unchanged.\",\n        \"No provider, state, credentials, deployment or publication operation.\"\n      ],\n      \"oracle\": \"Actual native built artifacts run in workerd; real Chromium independently confirms the exact RPC endpoint, no initial/replayed call, no trace/cookie headers and the retained answer. The API artifact contains the engine marker while browser artifacts must not. The generated native settings identity, short request marker and source-built internal defect require actual responses and positive fixed reporting; removing the owning failure boundary makes marker reflection fail the saved test. Unknown native function-address requests must return empty 404 and must omit the short request marker from actual native logs; removing exact-address admission restores that log leak. Actual built API global/procedure/fatal replies use fixed safe values; expected/version errors retain checked identity. A source-built damaged valid-JSON reply must restore a checked error through the genuine Website binding, with real Chromium editing and no replay. Positive fixed host logs omit the marker and pay values. Removal of each native encoder or the owned reply decoder must fail the saved test, followed by exact restoration and fresh dependency/artifact builds. Controlled API roots retain the real calculation/encoding and delay headers or the remaining body for twelve seconds. Actual generated clients must hit the ten-second deadline; Chromium must observe request abort after deadline, editing and actual Back route departure. Removing deadline or edit interruption fails the saved test; exact restoration and fresh builds pass. Pay-value checks inspect emitted log messages; private text checks inspect the whole record. Actual native mock-plan properties and saved real CLI state must contain the disabled collection policy; removing the API graph property fails the saved state Schema after runtime checks. These are declared-state checks, not cloud upload or exported-row proof. An actual successful browser answer survives edits, controlled unavailable retry and invalid form without being presented as current. Reverting figures makes no request and still needs one explicit real RPC to clear the stale message. Actual Worker-generated successful submission HTML hydrates without replay and retains its answer through editing and failed retry. The additional pages must independently return both known results via real API artifacts; no calculation fixture supplies them. Each page starts without the previous calculator's answer. Saved forms and report identity are checked together. Exact browser locator fill admissions have actual CLI positive and neighbouring-application negative fixtures. The size oracle uses multi-byte text below 65536 characters but above 65536 encoded bytes at both API paths and all three form paths. API boundary fixtures also accept exactly 65536 bytes and reject progressive streams without reading their tail. The bounded private client must classify an actual native 413 as the checked request-size error. Valid native calculator/catalogue replies at exactly 2 MiB succeed; over-limit streams stop before the tail and release. Status fixtures prove request-controller abort, safe serialized guidance and one call only. Six restored checked error variants hydrate with their guidance and no new calculation. The built shared-work fixture reaches eight calculations across one HTTP call and a seven-item RPC batch, refuses extra HTTP/SSR/public browser work, retains manual-retry guidance with no edit replay, emits checked HTTP 504/RPC timeouts at five seconds and reaches cleanup. The actual generated client preserves timeout identity. Direct scoped tests prove cancelled/failed place reuse and independent instance pools; timers do not claim forced CPU pre-emption. The owning native pair also reads detail/schema/graph/facts/rules/jurisdictions/tax years from the actual API artifact. The shared RPC corpus proves decoder, size, status, deadline, interruption and old-revision rejection for every named call. Documentation assertions inspect actual initial HTML for every page before independent Chromium navigation. Three source-built API variants retain valid checked pages but change Markdown, metadata or module identity; cold Website SSR and the actual native GET must detect each mismatch. A genuine server-function response is damaged in the browser to prove restoration rejects it. The API artifact must positively contain the executable calculator service identity and browser chunks must omit it; accepted documentation prose cannot stand in for an engine marker. Full-page images supplement functional observations only. Search SSR titles must match real built API results; the original URL resists a forged header. Native function identity is read from its compiled owner. A damaged genuine search reply must fail restoration. Actual form/result navigation and JavaScript-free submission are independently observed in Chromium. Focused browser navigation waits for rendered words before asserting checked outcomes; a bare router promise is insufficient. Bounded startup readiness cannot hide application errors or a persistent gateway failure.\",\n      \"environment\": \"Local TaxKit checkout, native workerd and Chromium\",\n      \"authority\": \"none\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-website-failures.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-local-development.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-native-trace-containment.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-stale-calculator-answer.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-take-home-explanation.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-catalogue-rpc.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculator-pages.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-request-body-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-client-response-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-05-calculation-work-policy.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-closed-rpc-operations.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-06-request-operation-protections.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-connection.json\",\n        \"docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-search.json\"\n      ],\n      \"nonClaims\": [\n        \"No cloud provider, deployed endpoint or trace-export proof; controlled native fatal/privacy paths are qualified only by the named local tests.\",\n        \"Public and private API requests use separate local isolates from the same API artifact; caller upload cancellation is not established.\",\n        \"Browser/caller abort does not establish cancellation of the upstream artificial delayed Worker response.\"\nsed: docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation/tasks.json: No such file or directory\nreceipt was untracked during the earlier local path checks and staged later,\nso those checks did not cover it. The corrected portable report replaces only\nthose roots with descriptive markers, retains the original isolated report\nhash and records the projected hash. Product source, catalogue, compiled\nartifacts, reading findings and capture bytes are unchanged. The earliest\nchecking owner now states that new retained receipts must be staged before\nthe final tracked-file check. The existing checker and its scope are preserved.\n\nDocumentation impact: Change required for this receipt, the testing/quality\nowner and active plan; Preserve for product/runtime source and accepted\ncontent, review findings, tax results and prior immutable receipts; N/A for\npackage contract, Changeset, operational procedure and provider state. Focused\nchecks and corrected-commit hosted proof are recorded separately; earlier\nfull local qualification does not establish hosted success. T005 remains in\nprogress and metrics remain deferred.\n\n### T005 Website search implementation — 7 October\n\nThe next bounded slice connects a human search page to the existing named\n`searchDocs` operation and accepted catalogue. A plain GET form keeps search\nusable without JavaScript; results use the existing document link behaviour.\nThe original address owns SSR words, while the generated native browser GET\ncarries only a bounded ASCII URI component header. The installed native URI\ncodec carries Unicode, and the owning content Schema retains the 100-character\nterm, 20-result and 240-character excerpt limits. Empty, missing, invalid,\nloading and unavailable states remain distinct. No separate search index,\ncollection event or personalised content is introduced.\n\nDocumentation impact before acceptance: Change required for Website source,\nSchema/route/host ingress, exact route-consumer lint proof, native reading/search\njourney, Website/frontend/content/API/testing owners, SPEC/task and this plan;\nPreserve for accepted source/review/navigation, content service/RPC contract,\nretained results and disabled collection; N/A for a new package export,\nChangeset, deployment procedure, provider or credential operation. Discovery,\nMarkdown negotiation, images and old-app retirement remain later T005 work.\n\n\nThe search router now preserves literal URL pairs: the framework's default\nJSON parser changed `1e3` into `1000`. The focused fixture uses the actual\nsearch loader/components with a plain shell because the browser runner already\nowns an HTML document; it waits for rendered words after navigation before\nasserting checked outcomes. Human results show accepted titles/descriptions;\nraw Markdown excerpts remain an API contract and are not displayed as prose.\n\nHosted Quality run `37500299332` for `b7cbed17` failed on the real CLI\nfixture's initial Website navigation: 502 instead of 200 after API health\nsucceeded. Its retained hosted excerpt identifies no underlying cause. The\nfixture now observes served-page readiness after printed addresses, retrying\nonly 502/503 for fifteen seconds before a strict 200 browser navigation.\nOther errors remain failures. Qualification and later hosted status must be\nrecorded separately; the earlier failed run is not reclassified as success.\n\n\nThe first full search verification passed the complete tests and workflow\nfailure-canaries, then caught a browser-fixture type clash: Bun's HTML-rewriter\n`Element.append` accepts text/streams rather than a DOM node. The fixture only\nneeds its own rendered values, so its scoped React shell remains detached.\nNo cast, lint exception or global type override is added. Real page, focus and\nform observations remain in the native journey. Fresh focused types, lint and\nbrowser checks precede complete qualification of the corrected sources.\n### T005 discovery implementation intent — 7 October\n\nSearch commit `8b32afca` passed complete local tests and verification and was\npushed to draft #155. Its own hosted Quality run `37509022712` remains pending\nat this observation. Metrics remain deferred.\n\nThe next slice derives `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt` and\n`/llms-full.txt` from the accepted catalogue in the backend content owner.\nNative Website addresses are deferred `Worker.URL` values, so the ordinary\nsource build cannot safely bake the actual stage origin into static files.\nOne closed discovery operation will use the application's already checked,\ncached Website settings at request time; the Website will return its checked\ndocument without owning a second catalogue or reading authored MDX. Public\norigin validation will have one shared Schema with separate API and Website\nidentities. No calculation values, invented modification dates, additional\ncache or collection event belong in these files.\n\nThe current llms.txt proposal, sitemap protocol and Google's crawler guidance\nwere read on 7 October. Agent links must lead to usable processed Markdown;\nthe current explicit API Markdown links can do this while same-page Markdown\nnegotiation remains a later slice. Robots controls crawling rather than access;\nsearch retains its noindex response/page policy. The actual configured origin,\ncomplete accepted-page coverage, text/media types, safe errors, request lifetime\nand old useful routes need local built-app proof before accepting this slice.\n\nDocumentation impact: Change required for content/API/RPC/Website contracts,\ntheir package guides, owning architecture, exact checks and current task/journey\npointers. Preserve source-bound acceptance, retained tax results, previous proof,\ndisabled collection and the older app until retirement proof. No new operational\ncommand or provider action is intended, so runbook applicability is N/A.\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"documentType\": \"bounded-proof-receipt\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"evidence\",\n  \"authority\": \"supporting\",\n  \"owner\": \"taxkit-web-app-owner\",\n  \"observedAt\": \"2026-10-06T18:07:15.169711+00:00\",\n  \"status\": \"Local Website accepted-catalogue search qualified; whole T005 remains in progress\",\n  \"baseHead\": \"b7cbed17a0b52283b5f9f75abf68c448d73af390\",\n  \"actorAuthority\": {\n    \"principal\": \"Cooper\",\n    \"reviewer\": \"Codex\",\n    \"operation\": \"Approved CSF-T005 implementation, local checks, tested commit/push and continuation of draft PR155\",\n    \"environment\": \"Local native workerd/Chromium pair and repository checks\",\n    \"approvalBoundary\": \"No merge, deploy, publication, provider apply or metrics implementation\"\n  },\n  \"outcome\": [\n    \"A labelled /search GET form uses the existing accepted-catalogue searchDocs operation, works without JavaScript and links checked title/description results to documentation.\",\n    \"Literal URL pairs preserve scientific numbers, quoted words, duplicate keys and Unicode; checked ingress rejects unexpected/duplicate keys and overlong words.\",\n    \"Generated native search GET takes no data or client Context, carries only a bounded ASCII URI header and decodes Unicode through the installed Schema codec. Original SSR URLs resist forged headers.\",\n    \"Empty words skip search. Empty/no-match/loading/invalid/unavailable states remain separate; damaged genuine browser replies fail checked restoration safely.\",\n    \"The route restores and matches encoded results before readonly leaf composition. Typed route context avoids server imports in a browser route. Existing heading-focus and phone navigation remain owned.\",\n    \"Local startup observes served-page readiness after printed addresses, retrying only 502/503 for at most fifteen seconds before strict successful browser navigation. The earlier hosted 502 cause remains unknown.\"\n  ],\n  \"impact\": {\n    \"changeRequired\": [\n      \"apps/web source/Schema/UR