{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:40:55.160Z","ordinal":50600,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac54090b89c87d096651ec10f42fd8a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_9xqPVJEhkE0bQ58oZ70SQ3W1","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py <<'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nimport json,re\\nreceipt='docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json'\\ndef edit(p,a,b):\\n s=Path(p).read_text();assert a in s,(p,a);Path(p).write_text(s.replace(a,b,1))\\ndef add(p,s):\\n with Path(p).open('a') as f:f.write('\\\\n\\\\n'+s+'\\\\n')\\np='docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md'\\nedit(p,'connection changes no public HTTP/RPC contract. Discovery remains T005 work.','''connection preserves the four public HTTP content routes. The fifth named\\ndocumentation call changes the private documentation revision. It returns a\\nclosed discovery document derived from accepted content and the API application's\\nchecked, lazy cached stage settings; the client checks its returned file path\\nagainst the requested one. Shared origin validation has separate API/Website\\nidentities. The Website serves the four conventional files without reading MDX\\nsource or constructing another runtime.''')\\np='docs/architecture/frontend.md'\\nedit(p,'T005 now prepares four checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.','T005 now supplies five checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.')\\nedit(p,'Discovery and replacement qualification must\\\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.','Markdown negotiation, share images and replacement qualification must\\\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.')\\nedit(p,'four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.','five named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.')\\nedit(p,'Search is described below; discovery remains T005 work.','Search and discovery are described below; later T005 work remains open.')\\nedit(p,'introduced. Discovery files and share images remain separate T005 work.','introduced. Share images and Markdown negotiation remain separate T005 work.')\\nadd(p,'''### Replacement Website discovery files\\n\\nThe Website host admits four closed paths before React routing: `/sitemap.xml`,\\n`/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt` and `/llms-full.txt`. Its existing server runner calls\\n`docsDiscovery`, backed by the native API client and `ContentDiscovery` owner.\\nThe backend derives the file from the same accepted catalogue and checks lazy\\napplication settings for actual stage addresses. The Website owns no second\\nindex, authored-source access or live Layer construction.\\n\\nGET returns checked XML or plain text, UTF-8, a five-minute public cache and\\n`nosniff`. HEAD has the same headers, explicit 200 and no body. Other methods\\nreturn empty 405 with `Allow: GET, HEAD`; query input returns empty 400.\\nExpected transport/configuration failure gives empty 503 with `no-store`.\\nUnexpected Causes keep the existing safe host failure policy. The short agent\\nindex links existing public API processed Markdown; the full file preserves\\nall accepted bodies, including fenced code examples. No personal reports enter\\nthese documents. The [discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\\nowns bounded local observations; availability and old-app retirement require\\nseparate proof.''')\\np='docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md'\\nedit(p,'The documentation RPC corpus checks four named operations with a separate','The documentation RPC corpus checks five named operations with a separate')\\nedit(p,'below; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\\\\nremain unproved by these local slices.','below. Discovery files have their own qualification below; old-app retirement,\\\\ndeployment and public availability remain unproved by these local slices.')\\nadd(p,'''### Native Website discovery qualification\\n\\nContent tests derive all four closed documents from a checked synthetic\\ncatalogue and configuration, observe lazy cached settings, reject unsafe origins\\nand relate each path to its media type and body bound. The existing private RPC\\ncorpus covers the fifth operation, including malformed/oversized/status/fatal\\nreplies, deadlines, interruption and revision skew. A valid checked reply for a\\ndifferent file must be rejected; fixed discovery guidance cannot contain the\\nprivate source diagnostic.\\n\\nThe source-built native pair compares each Website GET body against the real\\nchecked API client and accepted catalogue, checks all 61 canonical sitemap\\naddresses and parses XML in Chromium. It checks actual GET/HEAD media/cache/\\n`nosniff` headers, explicit empty 200 HEAD, method/query rejection and a real\\nunavailable binding's empty uncached 503. Exact processed Markdown comparison\\npreserves useful imports inside fenced code examples; an assertion rejecting\\nall import lines would falsely reject accepted documentation. Existing source\\ncompilation owns removal of authored MDX syntax. Retained source hashes qualify\\nsource preservation separately. The [dated discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\\nrecords candidate identities, corrections and actual check results; it does not\\nclose T005, establish deployment or prove the later Markdown/image/retirement\\nwork.''')\\nadd('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','''## T005 discovery contract\\n\\nThe backend content owner projects `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt`\\nand `/llms-full.txt` from the same accepted catalogue. Application composition\\nprovides lazy cached, checked API and Website stage origins; native deferred\\naddresses cannot be guessed during an ordinary source build. A shared secure\\nroot-origin Schema retains separate semantic identities. The closed discovery\\nSchema owns the exact path/media relationship and a 300,000-character body\\nbound within the existing two-MiB private reply budget.\\n\\nThe fifth documentation RPC operation uses revision 2 and checks the reply path\\nagainst the requested one. Calculator revision 4 and four public HTTP content\\nroutes stay unchanged. The Website's existing runner serves checked GET files\\nand explicit empty 200 HEAD with the same headers. Unexpected methods/query and\\nunavailable settings/binding have empty safe 405/400/503 responses. Sitemap XML\\ncontains all accepted canonical addresses with no guessed modification date.\\nShort agent links use the existing processed-Markdown API endpoint; the full\\nindex preserves all processed bodies and useful fenced code examples. No\\ncalculation report, second content index or collection event is introduced.\\n\\nThe existing native journey checks actual built API/Website files, XML parsing,\\nall accepted content, correct media/cache headers and safe failure paths. T005\\nremains in progress for same-page Markdown negotiation, share images and\\nold-app retirement. Metrics remain deferred.''')\\np='docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md'\\nedit(p,'Four separately versioned native documentation RPC operations are the current candidate. Replacement Website routes and discovery remain unfinished.','Pages and search passed local qualification. Five separately versioned native documentation RPC operations and four conventional discovery files are the current candidate. Markdown negotiation, share images and old-app retirement remain unfinished.')\\nadd(p,'''The final scope uses only the new private discovery call and conventional\\nWebsite file URLs. An exploratory public HTTP JSON discovery route was removed:\\nexisting public Markdown links already serve the short index, so that extra\\nroute added no needed consumer. The four public HTTP content routes, accepted\\nsource/review records and generated OpenAPI owner stay unchanged. Content and\\nprivate RPC have appropriate major Changesets for their new contracts.\\n\\nThe first native attempt exposed HEAD's default empty 204 response; its host\\nowner now explicitly returns 200 with GET-equivalent headers. The next attempt\\nfound an invalid full-index assertion that rejected imports inside useful fenced\\ncode examples. Exact accepted processed-body comparison replaces that assertion;\\nsource compilation retains responsibility for removing authored MDX syntax.\\nNo cast, policy exception or tax-data change is added. Current qualification is\\npending at the [discovery receipt](../../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json).''')\\np='docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());t=next(t for t in v['tasks'] if t['id']=='CSF-T005');assert t['status']=='in_progress'\\nt['evidence'].append(receipt)\\nt['browserVerification'][1]='Check draft exclusion and removal of authored MDX syntax while preserving useful fenced code examples; valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.'\\nPath(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\np='docs/verification/critical-journeys.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());j=next(j for j in v['journeys'] if j['id']=='taxkit-native-website');j['expectedBehavior'].append('Four conventional discovery files derive from the accepted catalogue and checked stage origins through the private API client; actual GET/HEAD headers and bodies, XML parsing, all canonical addresses and safe unavailable/method/query responses hold.')\\nj['oracle']+=' Actual built discovery GET bodies must equal the checked native client documents. Chromium XML parsing must produce the sitemap namespace and all 61 canonical addresses in catalogue order. Explicit HEAD 200 must have an empty body and GET-equivalent headers. A real unavailable API binding must return empty uncached 503. The actual RPC corpus rejects a valid document for a different requested path.'\\nj['evidence'].append(receipt);Path(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nPath(receipt).write_text(json.dumps({'schemaVersion':1,'documentType':'bounded-proof-receipt','lifecycle':'inconclusive','authority':'supporting','owner':'taxkit-web-app-owner','observedAt':'2026-10-06T20:00:00Z','status':'Current discovery candidate awaits fresh focused and full local qualification','baseHead':'8b32afcae9bd3ac7a93e8d2f63143bc603717961','nonClaims':['No whole T005 completion, hosted success, deployment, publication or provider apply; metrics remain deferred.'],'resumeTrigger':'Fresh current-candidate checks, parent diff review and full qualification; replace this pending receipt before accepting this slice.'},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\\nfor p in ['packages/content/README.md','packages/api/rpc/README.md','apps/api/README.md','apps/web/README.md','docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md','docs/architecture/frontend.md','docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md','docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md','docs/architecture/package-ownership.md','docs/architecture/effect-services.md','docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md']:\\n s=Path(p).read_text();s=re.sub(r'(?m)^last_reviewed: .*$', 'last_reviewed: 2026-10-07',s);Path(p).write_text(s)\\nprint('Discovery owners and pending receipt updated')\\nPY\\npython3 /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py\",max_output_tokens:1000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","create_time":1791312014.799499}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:40:55.171Z","ordinal":50601,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","session_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","root_turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","response_id":"resp_02692a5b008ee3bd016ac5408e956087d0a7f9d0cf7573f565","usage":{"input_tokens":74603,"cached_input_tokens":73216,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2410,"reasoning_output_tokens":17,"total_tokens":77013},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":126089872,"cached_input_tokens":123576064,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":688354,"reasoning_output_tokens":333804,"total_tokens":126778226},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":961476411,"cached_input_tokens":941414528,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4631334,"reasoning_output_tokens":2012848,"total_tokens":966107745}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-06T18:40:55.283Z","ordinal":50602,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1055e-4560-7b33-82d2-226827c76159","turn_id":"01a110dd-a561-7f92-9e34-cf5bd1e8dee9","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-60582766-0d57-4c06-8993-d5fc97235454","process_id":"55852","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","cat > /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,re\nreceipt='docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json'\ndef edit(p,a,b):\n s=Path(p).read_text();assert a in s,(p,a);Path(p).write_text(s.replace(a,b,1))\ndef add(p,s):\n with Path(p).open('a') as f:f.write('\\n\\n'+s+'\\n')\np='docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md'\nedit(p,'connection changes no public HTTP/RPC contract. Discovery remains T005 work.','''connection preserves the four public HTTP content routes. The fifth named\ndocumentation call changes the private documentation revision. It returns a\nclosed discovery document derived from accepted content and the API application's\nchecked, lazy cached stage settings; the client checks its returned file path\nagainst the requested one. Shared origin validation has separate API/Website\nidentities. The Website serves the four conventional files without reading MDX\nsource or constructing another runtime.''')\np='docs/architecture/frontend.md'\nedit(p,'T005 now prepares four checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.','T005 now supplies five checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.')\nedit(p,'Discovery and replacement qualification must\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.','Markdown negotiation, share images and replacement qualification must\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.')\nedit(p,'four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.','five named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.')\nedit(p,'Search is described below; discovery remains T005 work.','Search and discovery are described below; later T005 work remains open.')\nedit(p,'introduced. Discovery files and share images remain separate T005 work.','introduced. Share images and Markdown negotiation remain separate T005 work.')\nadd(p,'''### Replacement Website discovery files\n\nThe Website host admits four closed paths before React routing: `/sitemap.xml`,\n`/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt` and `/llms-full.txt`. Its existing server runner calls\n`docsDiscovery`, backed by the native API client and `ContentDiscovery` owner.\nThe backend derives the file from the same accepted catalogue and checks lazy\napplication settings for actual stage addresses. The Website owns no second\nindex, authored-source access or live Layer construction.\n\nGET returns checked XML or plain text, UTF-8, a five-minute public cache and\n`nosniff`. HEAD has the same headers, explicit 200 and no body. Other methods\nreturn empty 405 with `Allow: GET, HEAD`; query input returns empty 400.\nExpected transport/configuration failure gives empty 503 with `no-store`.\nUnexpected Causes keep the existing safe host failure policy. The short agent\nindex links existing public API processed Markdown; the full file preserves\nall accepted bodies, including fenced code examples. No personal reports enter\nthese documents. The [discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\nowns bounded local observations; availability and old-app retirement require\nseparate proof.''')\np='docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md'\nedit(p,'The documentation RPC corpus checks four named operations with a separate','The documentation RPC corpus checks five named operations with a separate')\nedit(p,'below; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\\nremain unproved by these local slices.','below. Discovery files have their own qualification below; old-app retirement,\\ndeployment and public availability remain unproved by these local slices.')\nadd(p,'''### Native Website discovery qualification\n\nContent tests derive all four closed documents from a checked synthetic\ncatalogue and configuration, observe lazy cached settings, reject unsafe origins\nand relate each path to its media type and body bound. The existing private RPC\ncorpus covers the fifth operation, including malformed/oversized/status/fatal\nreplies, deadlines, interruption and revision skew. A valid checked reply for a\ndifferent file must be rejected; fixed discovery guidance cannot contain the\nprivate source diagnostic.\n\nThe source-built native pair compares each Website GET body against the real\nchecked API client and accepted catalogue, checks all 61 canonical sitemap\naddresses and parses XML in Chromium. It checks actual GET/HEAD media/cache/\n`nosniff` headers, explicit empty 200 HEAD, method/query rejection and a real\nunavailable binding's empty uncached 503. Exact processed Markdown comparison\npreserves useful imports inside fenced code examples; an assertion rejecting\nall import lines would falsely reject accepted documentation. Existing source\ncompilation owns removal of authored MDX syntax. Retained source hashes qualify\nsource preservation separately. The [dated discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\nrecords candidate identities, corrections and actual check results; it does not\nclose T005, establish deployment or prove the later Markdown/image/retirement\nwork.''')\nadd('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','''## T005 discovery contract\n\nThe backend content owner projects `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt`\nand `/llms-full.txt` from the same accepted catalogue. Application composition\nprovides lazy cached, checked API and Website stage origins; native deferred\naddresses cannot be guessed during an ordinary source build. A shared secure\nroot-origin Schema retains separate semantic identities. The closed discovery\nSchema owns the exact path/media relationship and a 300,000-character body\nbound within the existing two-MiB private reply budget.\n\nThe fifth documentation RPC operation uses revision 2 and checks the reply path\nagainst the requested one. Calculator revision 4 and four public HTTP content\nroutes stay unchanged. The Website's existing runner serves checked GET files\nand explicit empty 200 HEAD with the same headers. Unexpected methods/query and\nunavailable settings/binding have empty safe 405/400/503 responses. Sitemap XML\ncontains all accepted canonical addresses with no guessed modification date.\nShort agent links use the existing processed-Markdown API endpoint; the full\nindex preserves all processed bodies and useful fenced code examples. No\ncalculation report, second content index or collection event is introduced.\n\nThe existing native journey checks actual built API/Website files, XML parsing,\nall accepted content, correct media/cache headers and safe failure paths. T005\nremains in progress for same-page Markdown negotiation, share images and\nold-app retirement. Metrics remain deferred.''')\np='docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md'\nedit(p,'Four separately versioned native documentation RPC operations are the current candidate. Replacement Website routes and discovery remain unfinished.','Pages and search passed local qualification. Five separately versioned native documentation RPC operations and four conventional discovery files are the current candidate. Markdown negotiation, share images and old-app retirement remain unfinished.')\nadd(p,'''The final scope uses only the new private discovery call and conventional\nWebsite file URLs. An exploratory public HTTP JSON discovery route was removed:\nexisting public Markdown links already serve the short index, so that extra\nroute added no needed consumer. The four public HTTP content routes, accepted\nsource/review records and generated OpenAPI owner stay unchanged. Content and\nprivate RPC have appropriate major Changesets for their new contracts.\n\nThe first native attempt exposed HEAD's default empty 204 response; its host\nowner now explicitly returns 200 with GET-equivalent headers. The next attempt\nfound an invalid full-index assertion that rejected imports inside useful fenced\ncode examples. Exact accepted processed-body comparison replaces that assertion;\nsource compilation retains responsibility for removing authored MDX syntax.\nNo cast, policy exception or tax-data change is added. Current qualification is\npending at the [discovery receipt](../../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json).''')\np='docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());t=next(t for t in v['tasks'] if t['id']=='CSF-T005');assert t['status']=='in_progress'\nt['evidence'].append(receipt)\nt['browserVerification'][1]='Check draft exclusion and removal of authored MDX syntax while preserving useful fenced code examples; valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.'\nPath(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\n')\np='docs/verification/critical-journeys.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());j=next(j for j in v['journeys'] if j['id']=='taxkit-native-website');j['expectedBehavior'].append('Four conventional discovery files derive from the accepted catalogue and checked stage origins through the private API client; actual GET/HEAD headers and bodies, XML parsing, all canonical addresses and safe unavailable/method/query responses hold.')\nj['oracle']+=' Actual built discovery GET bodies must equal the checked native client documents. Chromium XML parsing must produce the sitemap namespace and all 61 canonical addresses in catalogue order. Explicit HEAD 200 must have an empty body and GET-equivalent headers. A real unavailable API binding must return empty uncached 503. The actual RPC corpus rejects a valid document for a different requested path.'\nj['evidence'].append(receipt);Path(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\n')\nPath(receipt).write_text(json.dumps({'schemaVersion':1,'documentType':'bounded-proof-receipt','lifecycle':'inconclusive','authority':'supporting','owner':'taxkit-web-app-owner','observedAt':'2026-10-06T20:00:00Z','status':'Current discovery candidate awaits fresh focused and full local qualification','baseHead':'8b32afcae9bd3ac7a93e8d2f63143bc603717961','nonClaims':['No whole T005 completion, hosted success, deployment, publication or provider apply; metrics remain deferred.'],'resumeTrigger':'Fresh current-candidate checks, parent diff review and full qualification; replace this pending receipt before accepting this slice.'},indent=2)+'\\n')\nfor p in ['packages/content/README.md','packages/api/rpc/README.md','apps/api/README.md','apps/web/README.md','docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md','docs/architecture/frontend.md','docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md','docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md','docs/architecture/package-ownership.md','docs/architecture/effect-services.md','docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md']:\n s=Path(p).read_text();s=re.sub(r'(?m)^last_reviewed: .*$', 'last_reviewed: 2026-10-07',s);Path(p).write_text(s)\nprint('Discovery owners and pending receipt updated')\nPY\npython3 /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py"],"cwd":"file:///Users/cooper/.codex/worktrees/aac7/taxkit","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"cat > /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,re\nreceipt='docs/documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json'\ndef edit(p,a,b):\n s=Path(p).read_text();assert a in s,(p,a);Path(p).write_text(s.replace(a,b,1))\ndef add(p,s):\n with Path(p).open('a') as f:f.write('\\n\\n'+s+'\\n')\np='docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md'\nedit(p,'connection changes no public HTTP/RPC contract. Discovery remains T005 work.','''connection preserves the four public HTTP content routes. The fifth named\ndocumentation call changes the private documentation revision. It returns a\nclosed discovery document derived from accepted content and the API application's\nchecked, lazy cached stage settings; the client checks its returned file path\nagainst the requested one. Shared origin validation has separate API/Website\nidentities. The Website serves the four conventional files without reading MDX\nsource or constructing another runtime.''')\np='docs/architecture/frontend.md'\nedit(p,'T005 now prepares four checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.','T005 now supplies five checked documentation calls at the API/RPC owner.')\nedit(p,'Discovery and replacement qualification must\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.','Markdown negotiation, share images and replacement qualification must\\nfinish before the retained docs app can retire.')\nedit(p,'four named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.','five named `WebsiteServerApplication` documentation operations.')\nedit(p,'Search is described below; discovery remains T005 work.','Search and discovery are described below; later T005 work remains open.')\nedit(p,'introduced. Discovery files and share images remain separate T005 work.','introduced. Share images and Markdown negotiation remain separate T005 work.')\nadd(p,'''### Replacement Website discovery files\n\nThe Website host admits four closed paths before React routing: `/sitemap.xml`,\n`/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt` and `/llms-full.txt`. Its existing server runner calls\n`docsDiscovery`, backed by the native API client and `ContentDiscovery` owner.\nThe backend derives the file from the same accepted catalogue and checks lazy\napplication settings for actual stage addresses. The Website owns no second\nindex, authored-source access or live Layer construction.\n\nGET returns checked XML or plain text, UTF-8, a five-minute public cache and\n`nosniff`. HEAD has the same headers, explicit 200 and no body. Other methods\nreturn empty 405 with `Allow: GET, HEAD`; query input returns empty 400.\nExpected transport/configuration failure gives empty 503 with `no-store`.\nUnexpected Causes keep the existing safe host failure policy. The short agent\nindex links existing public API processed Markdown; the full file preserves\nall accepted bodies, including fenced code examples. No personal reports enter\nthese documents. The [discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\nowns bounded local observations; availability and old-app retirement require\nseparate proof.''')\np='docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md'\nedit(p,'The documentation RPC corpus checks four named operations with a separate','The documentation RPC corpus checks five named operations with a separate')\nedit(p,'below; discovery assets, old-app retirement, deployment and public availability\\nremain unproved by these local slices.','below. Discovery files have their own qualification below; old-app retirement,\\ndeployment and public availability remain unproved by these local slices.')\nadd(p,'''### Native Website discovery qualification\n\nContent tests derive all four closed documents from a checked synthetic\ncatalogue and configuration, observe lazy cached settings, reject unsafe origins\nand relate each path to its media type and body bound. The existing private RPC\ncorpus covers the fifth operation, including malformed/oversized/status/fatal\nreplies, deadlines, interruption and revision skew. A valid checked reply for a\ndifferent file must be rejected; fixed discovery guidance cannot contain the\nprivate source diagnostic.\n\nThe source-built native pair compares each Website GET body against the real\nchecked API client and accepted catalogue, checks all 61 canonical sitemap\naddresses and parses XML in Chromium. It checks actual GET/HEAD media/cache/\n`nosniff` headers, explicit empty 200 HEAD, method/query rejection and a real\nunavailable binding's empty uncached 503. Exact processed Markdown comparison\npreserves useful imports inside fenced code examples; an assertion rejecting\nall import lines would falsely reject accepted documentation. Existing source\ncompilation owns removal of authored MDX syntax. Retained source hashes qualify\nsource preservation separately. The [dated discovery receipt](../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json)\nrecords candidate identities, corrections and actual check results; it does not\nclose T005, establish deployment or prove the later Markdown/image/retirement\nwork.''')\nadd('docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','''## T005 discovery contract\n\nThe backend content owner projects `/sitemap.xml`, `/robots.txt`, `/llms.txt`\nand `/llms-full.txt` from the same accepted catalogue. Application composition\nprovides lazy cached, checked API and Website stage origins; native deferred\naddresses cannot be guessed during an ordinary source build. A shared secure\nroot-origin Schema retains separate semantic identities. The closed discovery\nSchema owns the exact path/media relationship and a 300,000-character body\nbound within the existing two-MiB private reply budget.\n\nThe fifth documentation RPC operation uses revision 2 and checks the reply path\nagainst the requested one. Calculator revision 4 and four public HTTP content\nroutes stay unchanged. The Website's existing runner serves checked GET files\nand explicit empty 200 HEAD with the same headers. Unexpected methods/query and\nunavailable settings/binding have empty safe 405/400/503 responses. Sitemap XML\ncontains all accepted canonical addresses with no guessed modification date.\nShort agent links use the existing processed-Markdown API endpoint; the full\nindex preserves all processed bodies and useful fenced code examples. No\ncalculation report, second content index or collection event is introduced.\n\nThe existing native journey checks actual built API/Website files, XML parsing,\nall accepted content, correct media/cache headers and safe failure paths. T005\nremains in progress for same-page Markdown negotiation, share images and\nold-app retirement. Metrics remain deferred.''')\np='docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md'\nedit(p,'Four separately versioned native documentation RPC operations are the current candidate. Replacement Website routes and discovery remain unfinished.','Pages and search passed local qualification. Five separately versioned native documentation RPC operations and four conventional discovery files are the current candidate. Markdown negotiation, share images and old-app retirement remain unfinished.')\nadd(p,'''The final scope uses only the new private discovery call and conventional\nWebsite file URLs. An exploratory public HTTP JSON discovery route was removed:\nexisting public Markdown links already serve the short index, so that extra\nroute added no needed consumer. The four public HTTP content routes, accepted\nsource/review records and generated OpenAPI owner stay unchanged. Content and\nprivate RPC have appropriate major Changesets for their new contracts.\n\nThe first native attempt exposed HEAD's default empty 204 response; its host\nowner now explicitly returns 200 with GET-equivalent headers. The next attempt\nfound an invalid full-index assertion that rejected imports inside useful fenced\ncode examples. Exact accepted processed-body comparison replaces that assertion;\nsource compilation retains responsibility for removing authored MDX syntax.\nNo cast, policy exception or tax-data change is added. Current qualification is\npending at the [discovery receipt](../../documentation-audit/clean-slate-foundation/2026-10-07-website-docs-discovery.json).''')\np='docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.tasks.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());t=next(t for t in v['tasks'] if t['id']=='CSF-T005');assert t['status']=='in_progress'\nt['evidence'].append(receipt)\nt['browserVerification'][1]='Check draft exclusion and removal of authored MDX syntax while preserving useful fenced code examples; valid image output/size/cache, mobile/keyboard behaviour and old useful URL redirects.'\nPath(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\n')\np='docs/verification/critical-journeys.json';v=json.loads(Path(p).read_text());j=next(j for j in v['journeys'] if j['id']=='taxkit-native-website');j['expectedBehavior'].append('Four conventional discovery files derive from the accepted catalogue and checked stage origins through the private API client; actual GET/HEAD headers and bodies, XML parsing, all canonical addresses and safe unavailable/method/query responses hold.')\nj['oracle']+=' Actual built discovery GET bodies must equal the checked native client documents. Chromium XML parsing must produce the sitemap namespace and all 61 canonical addresses in catalogue order. Explicit HEAD 200 must have an empty body and GET-equivalent headers. A real unavailable API binding must return empty uncached 503. The actual RPC corpus rejects a valid document for a different requested path.'\nj['evidence'].append(receipt);Path(p).write_text(json.dumps(v,indent=2)+'\\n')\nPath(receipt).write_text(json.dumps({'schemaVersion':1,'documentType':'bounded-proof-receipt','lifecycle':'inconclusive','authority':'supporting','owner':'taxkit-web-app-owner','observedAt':'2026-10-06T20:00:00Z','status':'Current discovery candidate awaits fresh focused and full local qualification','baseHead':'8b32afcae9bd3ac7a93e8d2f63143bc603717961','nonClaims':['No whole T005 completion, hosted success, deployment, publication or provider apply; metrics remain deferred.'],'resumeTrigger':'Fresh current-candidate checks, parent diff review and full qualification; replace this pending receipt before accepting this slice.'},indent=2)+'\\n')\nfor p in ['packages/content/README.md','packages/api/rpc/README.md','apps/api/README.md','apps/web/README.md','docs/architecture/api-and-sdk.md','docs/architecture/frontend.md','docs/architecture/testing-and-quality.md','docs/architecture/content-and-posts.md','docs/architecture/package-ownership.md','docs/architecture/effect-services.md','docs/product-specs/clean-slate-foundation.md','docs/exec-plans/active/clean-slate-foundation.md']:\n s=Path(p).read_text();s=re.sub(r'(?m)^last_reviewed: .*$', 'last_reviewed: 2026-10-07',s);Path(p).write_text(s)\nprint('Discovery owners and pending receipt updated')\nPY\npython3 /private/tmp/dev76-discovery-docs.py"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Discovery owners and pending receipt updated\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Discovery owners and pending receipt updated\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":18083},"formatted_output":"Discovery owners and pending receipt updated\n"},"started_at_ms":1791312055283,"completed_at_ms":1791312055283}}
